ity, logging\n /db # models, session, migrations hooks\n /services # kb search, chat, feedback\n /schemas # pydantic v2\n /middleware # request id, logging\n /alembic\n Dockerfile\n pyproject.toml\n README.md\n /worker\n /app\n Dockerfile\n pyproject.toml\n README.md\n /admin-console\n /src\n /electron\n package.json\n vite.config.ts (or similar)\n electron-builder config\n README.md\n\n/infra\n /docker\n docker-compose.yml\n docker-compose.prod.yml\n postgres-init (optional)\n\n/scripts\n make_all.sh\n make_all.ps1\n doctor.sh\n backup.sh\n restore.sh\n\n/docs\n README.md\n ENV.md\n OPERATIONS.md\n KB_AUTHORING.md\n SECURITY.md\n\n/.github/workflows\n ci.yml\n release.yml\n\n.env.example\n.gitignore\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 2) BACKEND (FASTAPI) — FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nBuild a modular FastAPI app with:\n- JWT auth for admin/superadmin\n- RBAC roles: public (no auth), admin, superadmin\n- PostgreSQL with JSONB KB + FTS tsvector using \"simple\"\n- Logging", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part10\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_14_watany_guide_part11", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part11", "text": "+ request_id correlation\n- Consistent error responses\n\nEndpoints (fully implemented):\n\nPublic:\n- GET /health\n- GET /metrics (Prometheus metrics OR minimal counters; must be real)\n- GET /kb/search?q=&lang=ar|en&limit=&status=published(default)\n- GET /kb/card/{id}?lang=\n- POST /chat/ask (KB-based deterministic chatbot flow)\n\nAuth:\n- POST /auth/login (admin/superadmin login; JWT)\n\nAdmin:\n- GET /admin/kb/cards?status=&q=&page=&limit=\n- POST /admin/kb/cards (create draft)\n- PUT /admin/kb/cards/{id} (edit draft)\n- POST /admin/kb/cards/{id}/publish (publish workflow rules apply)\n- POST /admin/kb/cards/{id}/archive\n- GET /admin/feedback/queue?status=open|in_review\n- POST /admin/feedback/{id}/resolve (link existing OR create draft OR reject)\n- GET /admin/audit (read-only)\n\nSuperadmin:\n- GET /superadmin/doctor\n- POST /superadmin/backup\n- POST /superadmin/restore\n- GET /superadmin/metrics\n- GET /superadmin/audit\n\nChatbot behavior (deterministic, production-safe):\n1) Detect language (ar/en) by Unicode heuristic; allow override lang param.\n2) Search KB using Postgres FTS (\"simple\") over BOTH locales content.\n3) Compute confidence score from ts_rank_cd; define:\n - CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD env default 0.25\n - AMBIGUITY_DELTA env default 0.05\n4) Decision:\n A) If top_score >= threshold AND (top_score - second_score) > ambiguity_delta:\n - Answer using ONE best card (localized fields)\n - Include citations: [card_id, title]\n - Optionally add \"Related\" up to 2 cards (titles only)\n B) If top_score >= threshold AND (top_score - second_score) <= ambiguity_delta:\n - Ask exactly 1 clarifying question\n - Present two options (titles + ids) and ask user to choose\n - Create feedback ticket with suggested ids\n C) If top_score < threshold:\n - Out-of-scope check: if clearly not municipality services → refuse + redirect\n - Else: fallback + ask 1 clarifying question\n - Create feedback ticket\n5) Always log session + messages + kb_hit_ids + confidence.\n\nRate limiting:\n- Support Redis-backed limiter if REDIS_URL provided.\n- In dev, if no Redis, use in-memory token bucket (must be pluggable).\n- In prod compose, Redis is recommended; in docker-compose.prod.yml include Redis.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 3) DATABASE SCHEMA (POSTGRES) — MUST IMPLEMENT\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nUse SQLAlchemy 2.0 models + Alembic migrations.\n\nTables:\n\n1) kb_cards\n- id UUID PK\n- slug TEXT unique\n- status TEXT (draft|published|archived)\n- locales JSONB:\n {\n \"ar\": { \"title\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\", \"tags\": [\"...\"] },\n \"en\": { \"title\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\", \"tags\": [\"...\"] }\n }\n- sources JSONB nullable (refs/citations)\n- version INT\n- created_by UUID FK users.id nullable\n- updated_by UUID FK users.id nullable\n- created_at, upda", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part11\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_15_watany_guide_part12", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part12", "text": "ted_at\n- published_at nullable\n- published_by UUID FK users.id nullable\n- published_snapshot JSONB nullable (frozen content that is served when published)\n- fts TSVECTOR stored/generated using \"simple\":\n to_tsvector('simple', concat_ws(' ',\n coalesce(locales->'ar'->>'title',''),\n coalesce(locales->'ar'->>'summary',''),\n coalesce(locales->'ar'->>'body',''),\n coalesce(locales->'en'->>'title',''),\n coalesce(locales->'en'->>'summary',''),\n coalesce(locales->'en'->>'body','')\n ))\nIndexes:\n- GIN on fts\n- btree on status, slug\nRule:\n- Public endpoints serve ONLY published cards and use published_snapshot if present (preferred), else locales.\n- Editing a published card creates/continues a draft version and does not change published_snapshot until publish.\n\n2) chat_sessions\n- id UUID PK\n- created_at\n- meta JSONB (channel, user_agent, etc)\n\n3) chat_messages\n- id UUID PK\n- session_id FK\n- role TEXT (user|assistant)\n- lang TEXT (ar|en)\n- content TEXT\n- kb_hit_ids UUID[] nullable\n- confidence FLOAT\n- created_at\nIndexes: session_id, created_at\n\n4) feedback_queue\n- id UUID PK\n- session_id FK\n- question TEXT\n- lang TEXT\n- suggested_kb_ids UUID[] nullable\n- status TEXT (open|in_review|resolved|rejected)\n- resolution JSONB (action, notes, created_card_id, linked_card_id)\n- created_at, updated_at\n\n5) users\n- id UUID PK\n- email TEXT unique\n- password_hash TEXT (bcrypt)\n- role TEXT (admin|superadmin)\n- is_active BOOL default true\n- created_at\n\n6) audit_logs\n- id UUID PK\n- actor_user_id FK nullable\n- action TEXT\n- target_type TEXT\n- target_id UUID nullable\n- details JSONB\n- created_at\n\nOptional but recommended:\n7) system_events\n- id UUID PK\n- type TEXT (backup|restore|doctor|migration)\n- status TEXT\n- details JSONB\n- created_at\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 4) BACKEND IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nCoding rules:\n- Dependency injection for DB sessions.\n- Pydantic BaseSettings from env. Fail-fast on bad config.\n- Structured JSON logging.\n- Request-ID middleware: generate if absent; include in logs and responses.\n- Error responses: consistent JSON with code/message/request_id.\n\nSecurity:\n- bcrypt hashing\n- JWT: HS256, expiry, issuer/audience optional\n- Validate JWT_SECRET length >= 32 in non-dev. If too short → app refuses to start.\n- CORS configurable via env.\n\nSearch implementation:\n- /kb/search uses plainto_tsquery('simple', q) and ts_rank_cd ordering.\n- Returns {items:[{id, slug, title, summary, score}], total, took_ms}\n- Public searches only published; admin can pass status=all.\n\nPublishing workflow rules (must implement):\n- TWO_PERSON_PUBLISH env default false.\n- If TWO_PERSON_PUBLISH=true:\n - The user who created/edited the last draft cannot publish it (must be different admin or superadmin).\n- Always record audit_logs for create/edit/publish/archive/feedback resolve.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 5) WORKER SERVICE (", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part12\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_16_watany_guide_part13", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part13", "text": "BACKGROUND JOBS)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate /apps/worker Python service (same deps family) that runs scheduled jobs:\n- nightly VACUUM ANALYZE\n- retention cleanup for chat_messages older than RETENTION_DAYS_CHAT\n- daily metrics aggregation (counts into system_events or logs)\n\nImplement using APScheduler with:\n- /health endpoint\n- graceful shutdown\n- structured logs with request_id-like job_id\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 6) ADMIN CONSOLE (ELECTRON + REACT) — WINDOWS 11 READY\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nElectron desktop app + React UI with:\n- Login screen (store token securely: in-memory + optional encrypted storage; do not store plaintext passwords)\n- Dashboard: KPIs (total chats, open feedback, published cards)\n- KB Manager:\n - list/search cards\n - create/edit bilingual fields (AR/EN tabs)\n - publish/archive (respect two-person rule message)\n - show version + published_at\n- Feedback Queue:\n - list open/in_review\n - detail view: question, suggested KB matches, actions:\n A) link existing KB\n B) create new KB draft prefilled\n C) reject with notes\n- Superadmin panel:\n - Doctor checks display\n - Backup/Restore trigger + progress\n - Audit log viewer (filter by action)\n\nUI rules:\n- RTL support for Arabic.\n- Minimal and fast.\n- Config: API_BASE_URL stored in app settings with default from env.\n- Use electron-builder to package Windows installer (artifact produced in CI release workflow).\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 7) OPS: SELF-HEALING SCRIPTS + WINDOWS WRAPPER\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate /scripts/make_all.sh:\n- Checks prerequisites: docker + docker compose\n- Ensures .env exists; if missing copy from .env.example\n- Boots containers (postgres, redis optional, api, worker)\n- Runs alembic upgrade head\n- Seeds superadmin user if not exists (SUPERADMIN_EMAIL/PASSWORD)\n- Runs doctor checks:\n - API /health\n - DB connection\n - FTS index existence\n - Redis connectivity if REDIS_URL set\n- Self-healing behavior on failure (safe):\n - restart failing containers\n - re-run migrations\n - re-seed superadmin if needed\n - dump logs to /tmp/watanbot-logs-*.txt\n- Non-interactive when AUTO_APPROVE=true\n\nCreate /scripts/make_all.ps1:\n- Best-effort Windows wrapper:\n - If WSL present: call bash make_all.sh\n - Else: run docker compose commands + python alembic commands inside containers\n- Must be usable on Windows 11.\n\nCreate /scripts/doctor.sh, backup.sh, restore.sh:\n- backup.sh: pg_dump + gzip, rotate by days, optional encryption if BACKUP_ENCRYPTION=age|gpg and key vars provided\n- restore.sh: restore latest backup; only non-interactive when AUTO_APPROVE=true; otherwise refuse and print instructions\n- All scripts log actions and write system_events via API endpoint or direct DB insert.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 8) DOCKE", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part13\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_17_watany_guide_part14", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part14", "text": "R COMPOSE (LOCAL + PROD)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n/infra/docker/docker-compose.yml (dev):\n- postgres (volume)\n- api\n- worker\n- redis (optional, enabled by default in compose; app can run without it in dev)\n\nAdd healthchecks + depends_on.\n\nProvide Dockerfiles for api and worker.\n\ndocker-compose.prod.yml:\n- includes redis required\n- includes stricter env validation (APP_ENV=prod)\n- uses restart policies\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 9) CI/CD (GITHUB ACTIONS)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nci.yml (on PR):\n- python lint: ruff\n- typecheck: mypy (minimal config)\n- tests: pytest\n- docker build images (api, worker)\n- spin up postgres (and redis) services in CI\n- run alembic upgrade head\n- run integration tests hitting API endpoints\n\nrelease.yml (on main):\n- build & push docker images (use secrets)\n- build Windows admin installer via electron-builder\n- upload admin artifacts to workflow artifacts\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 10) TESTING — MUST SHIP\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\npytest tests must cover:\n- auth login success/failure\n- create KB card draft → publish → searchable\n- /kb/search ranked results\n- /chat/ask creates feedback item when no confident hit\n- ambiguity: close scores causes 1 clarifying question flow\n- RBAC: admin cannot access superadmin endpoints\n- publish two-person rule when enabled\n\nAdd a small seed KB set for tests.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 11) DOCUMENTATION (RUNBOOKS)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nProvide:\n- /docs/README.md quickstart\n- /docs/ENV.md env vars (dev vs prod notes)\n- /docs/OPERATIONS.md backups/restore/doctor/self-healing\n- /docs/KB_AUTHORING.md how to write bilingual cards + publishing rules\n- /docs/SECURITY.md JWT/roles/secrets/rate limiting\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 12) ENV VARS (EXAMPLE)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate .env.example with:\nAPP_ENV=dev\nPOSTGRES_HOST=postgres\nPOSTGRES_PORT=5432\nPOSTGRES_DB=watanbot\nPOSTGRES_USER=watanbot\nPOSTGRES_PASSWORD=change_me\nAPI_HOST=0.0.0.0\nAPI_PORT=8000\nJWT_SECRET=change_me_change_me_change_me_32_chars_min\nJWT_EXPIRES_MINUTES=120\nCORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000\nSUPERADMIN_EMAIL=superadmin@example.com\nSUPERADMIN_PASSWORD=ChangeThisNow!\nAUTO_APPROVE=false\nRETENTION_DAYS_CHAT=180\nBACKUP_DIR=./backups\nCONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.25\nAMBIGUITY_DELTA=0.05\nTWO_PERSON_PUBLISH=false\nREDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0\nBACKUP_ENCRYPTION=none # none|age|gpg\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# 13) ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (MUST PASS)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nRepo is “done” only if:\n- scripts/make_all.sh brings up a clean machine from zero with Docker.\n- Admin console can login, create/edit/", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part14\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_18_watany_guide_part15", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part15", "text": "publish KB cards, search, and resolve feedback.\n- /chat/ask works end-to-end with safe response policy + logging + feedback queue.\n- FTS uses \"simple\" and bilingual search works with Arabic and English terms.\n- Backups and restore scripts work (non-interactive only when AUTO_APPROVE=true).\n- CI passes.\n\nNow generate the full repository with all files and code.\n\n# ============================================================\n# END OF COPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — FULL PRODUCTION (HARDENED v2)\n# ============================================================\n\nYou said:\nbased on all previous discussions especially those lissted in the guide file and knowing that the chatbot was created with vs studio but missing kbs and featuring all requirements previously discussd , write a single script to be used in copilot window inside =vstudio to make sure the watanbot has all required features and fully functional and build the kb from stated sources\n\nChatGPT said:\n\nThought for 13s\n# ============================================================\n# COPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — WATANBOT FULL BUILD + KB INGESTION (PRODUCTION)\n# Target: Visual Studio / VS Code Copilot Chat (paste everything)\n# Goal: Make WatanBot fully functional end-to-end, including building the Knowledge Base from the stated sources.\n# ============================================================\n\nYou are GitHub Copilot acting as a principal engineer. The project already exists (built in Visual Studio) but is missing KBs and some modules. Your job is to:\n1) Audit the repo, identify missing pieces, and implement everything required below.\n2) Build the Knowledge Base (KB) from the provided sources and wire it into the chatbot.\n3) Ensure production-grade behavior, deterministic answers, and a safe fallback with feedback/self-learning.\n4) Deliver a fully working system with scripts, migrations, seeding, admin tools, and tests.\n\nIMPORTANT DELIVERY RULES:\n- Make NO breaking changes without providing migrations and compatibility shims.\n- If files exist, modify them; if missing, create them.\n- Do not leave core features as TODO. Implement them fully.\n- Any generated “KB build” must be repeatable (idempotent) and safe.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# A) PRODUCT SCOPE + RESPONSE POLICY (MUST ENFORCE)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nWatanBot scope: municipal/civic services + administrative procedures + retired military personnel and their families’ administrative entitlements (pensions/compensations/healthcare/schools) ONLY IF such knowledge exists in KB sources. If a question is outside scope, refuse politely and redirect to what WatanBot can help with.\n\nResponse policy (strict):\n- Never invent documents, fees, deadlines, offices, or steps.\n- Only answer with details that exist in KB sources.\n- If answering from KB: always cite card_id + title.\n- If low confidence: do NOT provide procedural steps; ask exactly 1 clarifying question and create feedback ticke", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part15\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_19_watany_guide_part16", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part16", "text": "t.\n\nChat response rules:\n- If one clear best result => answer using ONE best card + up to 2 “Related”.\n- If top 2 are close => ask 1 clarifying question and show 2 options only.\n- If below threshold => fallback + ask 1 clarifying question, open feedback ticket.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# B) HARD CONSTRAINTS (TECH)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nBackend:\n- FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2.x + Alembic + Pydantic v2\n- PostgreSQL\n- Full-Text Search MUST use to_tsvector('simple', ...) for bilingual indexing. NEVER 'arabic'.\n- Dependency injection for DB session\n- Structured JSON logging + request_id middleware\n- JWT Auth + RBAC: public, admin, superadmin\n- Rate limiting: Redis-backed if REDIS_URL exists; else dev in-memory limiter (pluggable)\n\nAdmin:\n- Electron + React desktop console for KB + feedback queue + superadmin ops\n- Windows 11 packaging via electron-builder\n\nOps:\n- Scripts: make_all.sh + make_all.ps1 + doctor + backup + restore\n- Docker Compose dev + prod\n- CI workflows: lint/test/migrations/build\n\nSelf-learning:\n- Feedback queue: low-confidence queries create tickets\n- Admin resolves: link existing KB or create new KB draft\n- Publishing: optional two-person approval controlled by env TWO_PERSON_PUBLISH=true\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# C) KNOWLEDGE BASE: WHAT YOU MUST BUILD\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nThe KB MUST be built from “stated sources” provided in the repo. Implement ingestion from a /sources directory.\nCreate and enforce this folder convention:\n\n/sources\n /primary\n - *.pdf\n - *.docx\n - *.txt\n - *.md\n /secondary\n - *.pdf/*.docx/*.txt/*.md\n sources.manifest.json # required metadata registry\n\nThe manifest is the single source of truth for KB ingestion. If it does not exist, create it with placeholder entries and document how the user should fill it.\nManifest schema:\n\n{\n \"version\": 1,\n \"default_language\": \"ar\",\n \"sources\": [\n {\n \"source_id\": \"municipality_services_2026\",\n \"tier\": \"primary\",\n \"path\": \"sources/primary/municipality_services.pdf\",\n \"title\": {\"ar\": \"...\", \"en\": \"...\"},\n \"publisher\": \"...\",\n \"published_date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\",\n \"scope_tags\": [\"municipality\", \"permits\", \"civil_registry\"],\n \"license\": \"internal\",\n \"ingest\": {\"enabled\": true, \"chunking\": \"semantic\", \"max_chunk_chars\": 1800}\n }\n ]\n}\n\nKB Storage model:\n- Store “KB cards” as JSONB with bilingual locales.\n- Each card includes: title, summary, body, tags, and a sources[] list referencing manifest source_id + page/section if available.\n- Cards are the only things the bot can answer from.\n\nKB Ingestion behavior:\n- Build cards by chunking each source into coherent sections (semantic heading-aware chunking for md/txt, page chunking for pdf, paragraph chunking for docx).\n- For each chunk, generate a card:\n - slug stable\n - locales.ar filled (and locales.en optional)", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part16\"}"}
