TEXT (ar|en)\n- content TEXT\n- kb_hit_ids UUID[] nullable\n- confidence FLOAT\n- created_at\n\n4) feedback_queue\n- id UUID PK\n- session_id FK\n- question TEXT\n- lang TEXT\n- suggested_kb_ids UUID[] nullable\n- status TEXT (open|in_review|resolved|rejected)\n- resolution JSONB\n- created_at, updated_at\n\n5) users\n- id UUID PK\n- email TEXT unique\n- password_hash TEXT\n- role TEXT (admin|superadmin)\n- is_active BOOL default true\n- created_at\n\n6) audit_logs\n- id UUID PK\n- actor_user_id FK nullable\n- action TEXT\n- target_type TEXT\n- target_id UUID nullable\n- details JSONB\n- created_at\n\nOptional:\n7) kb_ingest_runs\n- id UUID PK\n- started_at, finished_at\n- status TEXT\n- manifest_version INT\n- stats JSONB (cards_created, updated, skipped)\n- logs TEXT\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# E) API ENDPOINTS (MUST IMPLEMENT)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nPublic:\nGET /health\nGET /metrics\nGET /kb/search?q=&lang=ar|en&limit=\nGET /kb/card/{id}?lang=\nPOST /chat/ask {session_id?, question, lang?}\n\nAuth:\nPOST /auth/login\n\nAdmin:\nGET /admin/kb/cards?status=&q=&page=&limit=\nPOST /admin/kb/cards\nPUT /admin/kb/cards/{id}\nPOST /admin/kb/cards/{id}/pub", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part17\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_21_watany_guide_part18", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part18", "text": "lish\nPOST /admin/kb/cards/{id}/archive\nPOST /admin/kb/ingest/run # triggers ingestion from /sources + manifest\nGET /admin/kb/ingest/runs\nGET /admin/feedback/queue\nPOST /admin/feedback/{id}/resolve\nGET /admin/audit\n\nSuperadmin:\nGET /superadmin/doctor\nPOST /superadmin/backup\nPOST /superadmin/restore\nGET /superadmin/metrics\nGET /superadmin/audit\n\nChat behavior (deterministic):\n- Detect language by unicode heuristic; allow override.\n- Query KB with plainto_tsquery('simple', q)\n- Use ts_rank_cd score\nEnv:\nCONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD default 0.25\nAMBIGUITY_DELTA default 0.05\n\nDecision tree:\nA) top >= threshold and clear winner => answer from 1 card + cite.\nB) ambiguous => ask 1 clarifying question + show 2 options + create feedback ticket.\nC) low => refuse out-of-scope OR fallback + 1 clarifying question + feedback ticket.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# F) ADMIN CONSOLE (ELECTRON + REACT) (IF MISSING, CREATE)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nMust include:\n- Login\n- Dashboard KPIs\n- KB Manager (bilingual fields tabs, publish/archive, ingest-run button)\n- Feedback Queue resolution flows\n- Superadmin: doctor + backup/restore + audit viewer\n- RTL when Arabic selected\n- electron-builder packaging config + build scripts\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# G) OPS: DOCKER + SCRIPTS + CI (MUST HAVE)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n1) Docker Compose dev and prod:\n- postgres\n- api\n- worker (optional but preferred for scheduled jobs + ingestion queue)\n- redis (recommended; required in prod)\n\n2) scripts:\n- scripts/make_all.sh: boot, migrate, seed superadmin, run doctor, optionally ingest if AUTO_INGEST=true\n- scripts/make_all.ps1: Windows wrapper (WSL or native compose)\n- scripts/doctor.sh: checks api/db/fts/redis\n- scripts/backup.sh + restore.sh: pg_dump + gzip + rotation; non-interactive only if AUTO_APPROVE=true\n\n3) CI:\n- ruff + mypy + pytest\n- docker build\n- migration test\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# H) WORKER (IF MISSING, CREATE)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nA Python worker service with APScheduler that can:\n- run VACUUM ANALYZE nightly\n- prune old chat logs\n- run ingestion as a scheduled job if enabled\nExpose /health.\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# I) SEEDING + FIRST-RUN EXPERIENCE (CRITICAL)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nImplement:\n- Seed superadmin from env SUPERADMIN_EMAIL/SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD on first run (idempotent).\n- Provide a sample manifest and sample KB seed cards (2-3) so system is usable even before real sources are added.\n- Provide a command/API to ingest /sources.\n\nFirst-run acceptance:\n- make_all brings system up\n- admin logs in\n- admin runs ingest\n- /chat/ask returns a KB answer when applicable, else safe fallback and creates feedback ticket.\n\n# -----------------------------", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part18\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_22_watany_guide_part19", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part19", "text": "-------------------------------\n# J) IMPLEMENTATION STEPS (WHAT YOU MUST DO NOW)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n1) Scan existing repository:\n- Identify missing modules (kb, db, auth, admin UI, worker, scripts)\n- Print a concise “gap report” in docs/GAP_REPORT.md\n2) Implement backend:\n- models + migrations\n- routers\n- services: kb_search, chat_engine, feedback_service, ingest_service\n3) Implement ingestion:\n- read sources.manifest.json\n- extract text:\n - PDF: pdfplumber (or pypdf) (choose stable)\n - DOCX: python-docx\n - TXT/MD: plain read\n- chunking rules + content_hash dedupe\n- insert/update draft cards\n4) Implement admin console:\n- Electron + React UI fully wired\n5) Implement scripts and docker compose\n6) Add tests\n7) Document runbooks and env\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# K) ENV VARS (.env.example)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\nAPP_ENV=dev\nPOSTGRES_HOST=postgres\nPOSTGRES_PORT=5432\nPOSTGRES_DB=watanbot\nPOSTGRES_USER=watanbot\nPOSTGRES_PASSWORD=change_me\nAPI_HOST=0.0.0.0\nAPI_PORT=8000\nJWT_SECRET=change_me_change_me_change_me_32_chars_min\nJWT_EXPIRES_MINUTES=120\nCORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000\nSUPERADMIN_EMAIL=superadmin@example.com\nSUPERADMIN_PASSWORD=ChangeThisNow!\nAUTO_APPROVE=false\nRETENTION_DAYS_CHAT=180\nBACKUP_DIR=./backups\nCONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.25\nAMBIGUITY_DELTA=0.05\nTWO_PERSON_PUBLISH=false\nREDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0\nAUTO_INGEST=false\nAUTO_INGEST_ON_BOOT=false\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n# L) ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (MUST PASS)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------\n- scripts/make_all.sh brings everything up from zero with Docker.\n- Admin console can login and manage KB and feedback queue.\n- /admin/kb/ingest/run ingests from /sources using manifest and creates draft cards.\n- Publishing creates published_snapshot and public endpoints serve only published.\n- /kb/search works with Arabic and English queries and uses FTS 'simple'.\n- /chat/ask never invents details, cites KB cards, and logs feedback when low confidence.\n- CI passes.\n\nNow implement all of the above in the existing repo, creating missing files, updating existing ones, adding migrations, scripts, Docker, admin console, worker, and tests. Output the full file tree and file contents.\n\n# ============================================================\n# END\n# ============================================================\nIf you want this to immediately build the KB from your sources, make sure your repo has a /sources folder + sources.manifest.json with correct paths before you run ingestion.\n\nYou said:\n\nwhile taking into consideration the previously produced script , the main focus shold be on the attached chatbot guide txt that was built by summarizing all discussions to producea chatbot 'watanbot' intended for lebanese veterans, analyse attached file and rewrite the new script\n\nChatGPT said:\n\nThough", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part19\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_23_watany_guide_part20", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part20", "text": "t for 42s\nAccording to a document from February 2026, your WatanBot KB foundation is meant to be built around (1) the Retirees Guide procedures and their correlations and (2) a National Defense Law layer with full-text search and a procedure ↔ law mapping table, all packaged in a searchable KB (SQLite in v3, with FTS tables).\nchatbot guide\n\nchatbot guide\n\nBelow is a single Copilot “master script” you can paste into the Copilot window inside Visual Studio/VS Code. It’s written to make Copilot generate/patch everything needed so WatanBot becomes fully functional, and to ensure the KB is built from the stated sources (guide → procedures, MOD law → articles, plus mapping).\n\nCOPILOT MASTER SCRIPT — WatanBot Full Production (Lebanese Veterans KB + App)\n\nContext / Non-Negotiables\n- Project name: WatanBot (watanbot)\n- Purpose: Help Lebanese retired military personnel + their families with pensions, compensations, healthcare, schooling, “على العاتق”, inheritance/death procedures, and other official transactions.\n- Primary KB source: Retirees “guide” that contains 11 main sections and ~65 procedures (“transactions”), with extracted structured signals per entry (where to submit, tags, canonical required documents, time limits, LBP amounts, URLs/phones) AND a similarity/correlation graph (procedure ↔ procedure). (This is already summarized as v2/v3 KB assets.)\n- Legal KB layer: National Defense Law (159 articles) with full-text search and a mapping table from procedure → relevant law articles with relevance + rationale.\n- KB v3 database structure (must exist and be queryable):\n - Guide side: transactions, tx_fts, tx_links\n - Law side: law_sources, law_articles, law_fts\n - Mapping: tx_law_map\n- Retrieval must support:\n (1) Search a procedure by Arabic keywords and return top matches\n (2) For a selected procedure, return its linked law basis (mapped articles ordered by relevance)\n (3) Search inside National Defense Law articles\n (4) Suggest “related next steps” using tx_links (correlations)\n- Implementation requirement: do NOT copy long paragraphs from sources; store structured summaries + metadata. Prefer Arabic-first responses with optional English summary (toggle / param).\n- Admin: Provide an admin UI or admin endpoints to review and refine mapping quality (first-pass mapping is rule-assisted and must be editable/regeneratable).\n\nExisting KB expectations (must be honored)\n- SQLite KB file expected name (default): retired_military_chatbot_kb_v3_with_ndlaw.sqlite\n- Tables and purpose:\n - transactions (tx_no, title, structured summary, tags)\n - tx_fts (full text search over titles/summaries)\n - tx_links (procedure↔procedure correlations)\n - law_sources (source record)\n - law_articles (article_no, text_ar, etc.)\n - law_fts (full text search across law articles)\n - tx_law_map (tx_no, article_no, relevance, rationale)\n- Provide quick SQL parity with:\n - SELECT ... FROM tx_fts WHERE tx_fts MATCH 'وفاة ورثة' LIMIT 5;\n - SELECT ... FROM tx_law_map", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part20\"}"}
