rtual table) indexing law_articles.text_ar\n- Must be idempotent:\n - If tables exist: verify and do nothing\n - If partial: create missing pieces if AUTO_CREATE_KB=true; else error\n- Add triggers or rebuild steps:\n - Either (A) contentless external content tables + FTS rebuild function\n - Or (B) content stored directly in FTS with external content table references\nChoose the simplest stable FTS5 approach and document it.\n\n1.2) scripts/kb_v3/kb_ingest_transactions.py\n- Inputs: local structured files under /sources (no web):\n - preferred: sources/primary/transactions.csv + sources/primary/tx_links.csv\n - allow JSONL equivalent\n- Ingest into:\n - transactions\n - tx_links\n- Rebuild tx_fts after ingestion (full rebuild is fine).\n- Must be idempotent:\n - Upsert by tx_no\n - Replace tx_links for tx_no when --overwrite-links is set\n- Expected transaction fields:\n - tx_no, section, title_ar, summary_ar, body_ar (optional), where_to_submit, required_docs(json),\n time_limits, amounts_lbp, contacts(json), steps(json or text), tags(json array)\n\n1.3) scripts/kb_v3/kb_ingest_ndlaw.py\n- Inputs: local file(s) under /sources, described", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part37\"}"}
