{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_44_watany_guide_part41", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part41", "text": "on TEXT NULL,\n tags_json TEXT NULL,\n updated_at TEXT NULL\n- tx_links:\n tx_no TEXT,\n related_tx_no TEXT,\n weight REAL DEFAULT 0,\n reason TEXT NULL\n- law_sources:\n source_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n title_ar TEXT,\n publisher TEXT,\n published_date TEXT,\n path TEXT,\n created_at TEXT\n- law_articles:\n article_no INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n text_ar TEXT NOT NULL,\n title_ar TEXT NULL,\n source_id TEXT NULL\n- tx_law_map:\n tx_no TEXT,\n article_no INTEGER,\n relevance INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n rationale TEXT NULL,\n PRIMARY KEY (tx_no, article_no)\n\nFTS approach (simple and stable):\n- Use FTS5 contentless tables and manual inserts:\n CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE tx_fts USING fts5(tx_no, title_ar, summary_ar, body_ar, tags, tokenize='unicode61');\n CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE law_fts USING fts5(article_no, text_ar, tokenize='unicode61');\n- On rebuild, repopulate from base tables.\n\n1.2) scripts/kb_v3/kb_ingest_transactions.py\nPurpose:\n- Ingest retirees guide procedures into transactions + tx_links and rebuild tx_fts.\nInputs:\n- sources/primary/transactions.csv\n- sources/primary/tx_links.csv\n- OR paths specified in sources/sources.manifest.json\nBehavior:\n- Upsert by tx_no (idempotent).\n- Store JSON fields as JSON strings in *_json columns (validate JSON).\n- Rebuild tx_fts after ingestion (full rebuild OK).\n- Provide flags:\n --kb PATH (default env KB_SQLITE_PATH)\n --manifest sources/sources.manifest.json (optional)\n --overwrite-links (replace tx_links for tx_no set)\n- Output stats: inserted/updated/skipped and missing columns.\n\nCSV expectations (minimum):\ntransactions.csv:\n tx_no, section, title_ar, summary_ar, body_ar, where_to_submit, required_docs_json, time_limits, amounts_lbp, contacts_json, steps_json, tags_json\ntx_links.csv:\n tx_no, related_tx_no, weight, reason\n\n1.3) scripts/kb_v3/kb_ingest_ndlaw.py\nPurpose:\n- Ingest National Defense Law into law_sources + law_articles and rebuild law_fts.\nInputs:\n- One or more local files listed in sources/sources.manifest.json under a source_id like \"ndlaw\".\nParsing:\n- Split by \"المادة\" markers.\n- Normalize Arabic numerals to Western digits for article_no extraction.\n- Store full Arabic text in text_ar.\nIdempotent:\n- Upsert by article_no.\n- If --overwrite-source is set, delete existing law_articles for that source_id first.\nRebuild law_fts after ingestion.\n\n1.4) scripts/kb_v3/kb_generate_tx_law_map.py\nPurpose:\n- Generate FIRST-PASS tx_no ↔ article_no mappings (human-reviewable).\nAlgorithm:\n- For each transaction:\n - Build query string from title_ar + summary_ar + tags_json keywords\n - Run law_fts MATCH query (sanitize terms)\n - Score candidates (FTS5 bm25 if available; else heuristic by term overlap + article length)\n - Select top N (env MAP_TOP_N default 5)\n - Save to tx_law_map with:\n relevance 0–100\n rationale Arabic short: “ربط أولي بناءً على تطابق كلمات: ...”\nIdempotent:\n- --overwrite replaces mappings for affected tx_no\nReport:\n- mapping_count\n- coverage = count(tx with >=1 mapping)/total tx\n- list top unmapped s", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part41\"}"}
