eries OK.\n- mapping coverage > 0 on seeded data.\n- v3 endpoints return results.\n- chat answers from v3 KB and creates feedback on no match.\n- backup contains KB file.\n\nNow implement all Phase-3 scripts, manifests, sample seeds, backend wiring, ops updates, and docs exactly as above.\nEND.\n\nYou said:\nbased on all previous dicussions and based on we reache the level three of building the kb for watanbot , i need to write a single script to allow watan bot to build its kb primarly fom file named daleel that defines all needed info that a veteran or one of his family might need for his own knowldge\n\nChatGPT said:\nCOPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — LEVEL 3 KB BUILD (PRIMARY SOURCE: “DALEEL”) — WATANBOT\n\nRole: You are Copilot acting as a senior KB/data engineer + backend integrator.\nContext:\n- We are at Level 3 of WatanBot KB building.\n- Canonical KB is SQLite v3 (KB_SQLITE_PATH, default /data/kb.sqlite).\n- Required KB tables (must exist): transactions, tx_fts, tx_links, law_sources, law_articles, law_fts, tx_law_map.\n- WatanBot is for Lebanese retired military personnel and their families.\n- Primary KB source NOW is a local file named “daleel” (دليل) which contains all", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part43\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_47_watany_guide_part44", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part44", "text": "needed info a veteran/family may need.\n- No web calls. Only local file ingestion.\n- This script MUST be idempotent, safe, and fully automated.\n\nGOAL:\nImplement a single command workflow that:\n1) Detects the “daleel” file under /sources/primary (or user-provided path).\n2) Extracts and normalizes its content (PDF/DOCX/TXT/MD supported).\n3) Converts the daleel into structured “Transaction Cards”:\n - title_ar, summary_ar, body_ar\n - where_to_submit\n - required_docs\n - time_limits\n - amounts_lbp\n - contacts (phones/links)\n - steps\n - tags\n - section/category\n4) Inserts/updates the SQLite v3 KB:\n - Upsert transactions by tx_no or stable slug/id\n - Build tx_links by detecting correlations/triggers (marriage, divorce, death, child age 18/25, dependency “على العاتق”, etc.)\n - Rebuild tx_fts for search\n5) Produces ingestion outputs for auditability:\n - /sources/derived/transactions.csv\n - /sources/derived/tx_links.csv\n - /sources/derived/daleel_extract.txt (normalized text)\n - /docs/DALEEL_INGEST_REPORT.md (stats + errors + coverage)\n6) Runs KB diagnostics at the end and fails if KB is not searchable.\n\nIMPORTANT CONSTRAINTS:\n- Do NOT invent facts not present in daleel. If a field isn’t found, keep it NULL/empty and tag the card “needs_review”.\n- Do NOT store long verbatim text; store structured summaries and short body sections. Keep any preview snippets under 200–300 chars.\n- No autonomous legal mapping in this script unless law_articles already exist; if law_articles exist, optionally generate first-pass tx_law_map for daleel cards only.\n\n========================================================\nA) FILE DISCOVERY + MANIFEST\n========================================================\nCreate/ensure these folders:\n- sources/primary\n- sources/derived\n- docs\n\nDALEEL file discovery rules:\n- Prefer files named (case-insensitive): daleel.*, دليل.*, dalil.*\n- Supported extensions: .pdf .docx .txt .md\n- If multiple matches, pick the newest modified file.\n- Allow override via CLI: --daleel PATH\n- Update sources/sources.manifest.json (create if missing) by adding:\n { \"source_id\":\"daleel\", \"type\":\"pdf|docx|text|md\", \"path\":\"...\", \"tier\":\"primary\", \"scope_tags\":[\"veterans\",\"pensions\",\"compensations\",\"healthcare\",\"schools\",\"dependency\"] }\n\n========================================================\nB) IMPLEMENT NEW SCRIPTS (SINGLE ENTRYPOINT)\n========================================================\nCreate ONE main entrypoint:\n- scripts/kb_v3/ingest_daleel.py\n\nIt must:\n1) Precheck gate:\n - verify KB_SQLITE_PATH exists or AUTO_CREATE_KB=true\n - call scripts/kb_v3/kb_init_v3.py if needed\n2) Extract text from daleel:\n - PDF: use pdfplumber (preferred) or pypdf\n - DOCX: python-docx\n - TXT/MD: read as utf-8 (handle BOM)\n - Write normalized full text to sources/derived/daleel_extract.txt\n - Normalize:\n - Arabic digits to Western\n - whitespace cleanup\n - unify punctuation\n3) Segment into “units”:\n - If PDF/DOCX has heading", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part44\"}"}
