reate feedback ticket (human review).\n\nImplement “User Modes” (server-side per phone number):\n- mode = guided | advanced\n- default guided\n- advanced can be enabled by admin or by user sending “متقدم”.\n\nStore user preferences (Postgres table):\n- wa_users(phone_number PK, mode, language_pref, accessibility_flags, last_seen_at)\n\nAccessibility flags:\n- big_text (affects message formatting)\n- voice_preferred (ask to send voice notes)\n- caregiver_mode (answers also include “رسالة مختصرة للمرشد/الابن”)\n\n========================================================\nB) WHATSAPP BUSINESS API INTEGRATION (REALISTIC)\n========================================================\nCreate router: apps/api/routers/whatsapp.py\n\nEndpoints:\n- GET /whatsapp/webhook (verification challenge)\n- POST /whatsapp/webhook (incoming messages)\n\nProcessing:\n1) Parse inbound message types:\n- text\n- audio/voice note\n- image\n- document\n- location\n2) Normalize into a unified “UserInput” object:\n- user_id (phone)\n- text (if any)\n- media pointers (image/doc/audio IDs)\n- location (lat/lng/address)\n- language_guess, script_guess\n3) Pass through input normalization (Section D below", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part52\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_56_watany_guide_part53", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part53", "text": ").\n4) Route to chat engine with context:\n- If location provided: treat as “closest office / where to submit” context (but only if KB supports location).\n- If photo/document: ask user what the file is (unless OCR enabled).\n5) Send reply using WhatsApp outbound message schema:\n- Text reply always supported.\n- If interactive messages are enabled, send list/buttons for guided mode.\n\nOutbound “actions” (safe):\n- Provide tappable items where supported:\n - “Call” -> send phone number in international format + “اضغط للاتصال” text\n - “Open link” -> send URL\n - “Send location” -> ask user to share location\n - “Send photo of document” -> ask user to photograph\nWhatsApp cannot initiate a call; only provide tap-to-call.\n\nImplement provider wrapper:\n- apps/api/integrations/whatsapp_client.py\n- Env vars:\n WHATSAPP_TOKEN\n WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID\n WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN\n\n========================================================\nC) MULTIMODAL PIPELINE: PHOTOS, FILES, LOCATION, VOICE\n========================================================\n\nC1) Photos / Documents\n- Store media metadata in Postgres table:\n wa_media(id, phone_number, type, mime, wa_media_id, url(optional), status, created_at)\n- Provide a download step (WhatsApp media API):\n - fetch media URL using token\n - download to /data/media/<id>\n- OCR:\n - Implement as optional hook with feature flag OCR_ENABLED.\n - If OCR not enabled, respond:\n “وصلت الصورة. هل هي صورة هوية/إفادة/إيصال؟ اكتب 1 أو 2 أو 3…”\n- If OCR enabled:\n - Extract text then run same KB lookup.\n - Never treat extracted text as authoritative; ask confirmation.\n\nC2) Location\n- When location received:\n - Save in wa_users.last_location_json\n - Respond with:\n “شكراً. هل تريد أقرب مكتب/رقم هاتف/مواعيد؟ اختر 1/2/3”\n - If KB has office directories by region, use them.\n - Otherwise say:\n “الدليل الحالي لا يحتوي على توزيع جغرافي للمكاتب. هل تريد أن أرسل لك الجهة المختصة العامة؟”\n\nC3) Voice recognition\n- Implement provider interface:\n apps/api/integrations/stt_provider.py\n - class SpeechToTextProvider with transcribe(audio_path, lang_hint)\n- Provide two implementations:\n - DummyProvider (default): returns None and prompts user to type or resend as text.\n - ExternalProvider (placeholder): only enabled if STT_PROVIDER and API keys exist.\n- If transcription succeeds:\n - Treat as user text and continue.\n- Always keep messages short; confirm interpretation:\n “فهمت أنك تسأل عن: … هل هذا صحيح؟ 1 نعم / 2 لا”\n\nC4) Face recognition (optional, default OFF)\n- This is sensitive. Implement only as “face match for duplicate profile detection” with FACE_RECOGNITION_ENABLED=false by default.\n- If enabled:\n - Only store embeddings, not raw images (if legally allowed).\n - NEVER use it to approve entitlements.\n- If user requests identity proof, respond with safer flow:\n “لأسباب الخصوصية، سنعتمد رقم الهاتف والمستندات المطلوبة فقط.”\n\n========================================================\nD) INPUT NORMALIZATION: ARABIZI + KEYBOARD-LAYOUT G", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part53\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_57_watany_guide_part54", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part54", "text": "ARBAGE + YAMLI\n========================================================\nCreate module: apps/api/services/input_normalizer.py\n\nPipeline:\n1) Detect script mix:\n- Arabic letters present? Latin letters present? digits?\n2) Keyboard-layout “garble” detection:\n- If text contains many Latin letters but user language_pref=ar or common Arabic words pattern absent,\n try transliterating as “Arabic typed on EN keyboard”:\n - Use a static map for Arabic keyboard layout:\n Example: 'h'->'ا' (illustrative; implement full mapping table for Arabic 101)\n- Also handle “English typed on Arabic keyboard” reverse map.\n3) Arabizi transliteration:\n- Convert common Arabizi numerals:\n 2=ء, 3=ع, 5=خ, 6=ط, 7=ح, 8=ق, 9=ص\n- Convert sh/ch/kh/gh/th/dh patterns.\n- Output candidate Arabic string.\n4) Yamli-like suggestions:\n- Produce up to 2 candidate normalized texts:\n - normalized_primary\n - normalized_alt\n5) Confidence:\n- If normalization confidence low, ask the user:\n “هل تقصد: (1) … أم (2) … ؟”\n6) Always store original_text and normalized_text in chat logs.\n\nImplement function:\nnormalize_input(text, user_lang_pref) -> {\n original, normalized, candidates[], confidence, detected_layout: \"ar_on_en\"|\"en_on_ar\"|None, detected_form: \"arabic\"|\"arabizi\"|\"mixed\"\n}\n\n========================================================\nE) CHAT ENGINE UPDATE FOR ELDERLY UX\n========================================================\nModify chat engine to:\n- Use guided mode by default:\n - If message is short (“مرحبا”, “تقاعد”, “مساعدة”), respond with menu choices.\n- When returning procedure steps:\n - Split into multiple WhatsApp messages if long (max ~800 chars each).\n - Provide “Send 1 for next step”.\n- Always include “References”: tx_no / article_no for transparency.\n- If user sends file/photo:\n - Ask what it is (1 ID, 2 family book, 3 receipt, 4 other) and proceed accordingly.\n- Add “Caregiver summary” if caregiver_mode enabled:\n - One short line that can be forwarded.\n\n========================================================\nF) “USER-SIDE ACTIONS” VIA INTENTS (SAFE)\n========================================================\nImplement “ActionIntents” returned by chat:\n- call_phone: {number, label}\n- open_url: {url, label}\n- request_location: {}\n- request_photo: {doc_type_hint}\n- request_voice: {}\n- create_followup_ticket: {topic}\n\nIn WhatsApp:\n- Render as:\n - text + inline instructions + formatted phone number\n - interactive buttons if supported\n\nDo NOT claim the bot can initiate calls. Provide tap-to-call numbers and instructions.\n\n========================================================\nG) ADMIN SETTINGS FOR UX\n========================================================\nAdd admin-configurable settings table (Postgres):\n- app_settings(key PK, value_json)\n\nKeys:\n- guided_mode_default (true)\n- max_steps_per_message (3)\n- stt_enabled (false)\n- ocr_enabled (false)\n- face_recognition_enabled (false)\n- language_default (\"ar\")\n- arabizi_enabled (true)\n- keyboard_garble_fix_enabled (true)\n\nAdmin UI:", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part54\"}"}
