on, and maintenance tasks.\n2) Generates step-by-step runbook instructions based on the current system state (doctor outputs, env, KB status).\n3) Can execute ONLY safe, whitelisted server-side admin actions (KB diagnostics, export/import mapping CSV, run KB ingest, backup/restore, rotate logs) and otherwise provides instructions for user-side tasks.\n4) For “user-side tasks” (WhatsApp configuration, sending a photo, location share, tap-to-call testing, permissions), it provides guided checklists and verifies by asking the admin to confirm outcomes (since server cannot click on user’s phone).\n\nIMPORTANT SECURITY MODEL:\n- SuperAdmin Bot is NOT a general assistant.\n- It only has access to:\n - internal diagnostics endpoints (doctor)\n - KB stats endpoints\n - audit logs\n - whitelisted admin actions\n- It MUST be protected by RBAC: superadmin only.\n- It MUST NOT expose secrets, tokens, raw passwords, or full document contents.\n- It MUST log every action to audit_logs.\n- It MUST have “dry-run” mode by default for destructive operations.\n\n========================================================\nA) DATA MODEL (POSTGRES) FOR RUNBOOK COACHING\n==========================", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part55\"}"}
