, “next step pending”.\n\nReturn ActionIntents (call/link/location/upload) that WhatsApp can render as interactive flows (see #4).\n\n2) RAG 2.0: iterative retrieval + better ranking beats “one-shot top-k”\nStrong results now come from:\n\nquery expansion / rewriting\n\nre-ranking (cross-encoder style) after retrieval\n\niterative retrieval (retrieve → reflect → retrieve again) rather than one pass\nResearch and enterprise practice increasingly show these patterns boost faithfulness and relevance. \n\nUpgrade for WatanBot (best ROI)\n\nKeep SQLite FTS as fast first-stage retrieval.\n\nAdd a second-stage reranker (even a small model or rules-based scorer) to reduce wrong matches.\n\nAdd adaptive/iterative retrieval only when confidence is low: try 1 extra retrieval pass using extracted keywords (transaction title + tags).\n\n3) Better “chunking”: structure-aware / adaptive chunking reduces hallucinations\nRecent studies highlight that “chunking by structure” (headings/sections) and adaptive chunk sizes preserve meaning and improve retrieval quality. \n\nUpgrade for WatanBot\n\nYour Daleel-aware ingestion is already the right move.\n\nAdd “structure signatures” into the KB: section, tr", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part58\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_62_watany_guide_part59", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part59", "text": "ansaction number, anchors (المستندات المطلوبة / المهلة / الرسوم).\n\nStore a compact “answer template payload” per transaction so generation is mostly formatting, not freewriting.\n\n4) WhatsApp platform upgrades: interactive messages + rich media flows\nWhatsApp’s platform explicitly supports richer conversational flows (interactive messages, CTAs, rich media). Meta’s docs provide the interactive message types to guide low-literacy users. \n\nUpgrade for WatanBot\n\nDefault to guided mode:\n\ninteractive list for main intents (معاش/طبابة/مدارس/وفاة/على العاتق…)\n\nreply buttons for yes/no + “التالي”\n\nConvert long answers into step paging:\n\n“1 للخطوة التالية”\n\nAdd a “caregiver forward” one-liner after each answer.\n\n5) Voice agents stack matured: streaming STT + VAD + turn detection\nVoice pipelines are becoming a standard “stack” (VAD + streaming STT + orchestration). There’s also active research on low-latency end-to-end voice agent systems for telecom scenarios. \n\nUpgrade for WatanBot (WhatsApp voice notes)\n\nAdd VAD/turn detection for clean transcripts (even if not real-time).\n\nImplement STT provider interface + fallback:\n\nif transcription fails → ask for a short typed keyword or a second voice note.\n\nWhat I recommend upgrading in WatanBot now\nA) Retrieval / KB engine upgrades (highest impact)\nTwo-stage retrieval\n\nStage 1: SQLite FTS (fast)\n\nStage 2: rerank top 10 using:\n\nkeyword overlap with title/tags\n\nrecency/updated flag\n\nsection relevance (army_only vs all_security_forces)\n\nIterative retrieval\n\nIf top2 are close: rewrite query with detected keywords (e.g., “وفاة + ورثة + معاش”) and run one more retrieval pass. \n\nAnswer-by-template\n\nGenerate responses from structured fields (docs/fees/deadlines/steps) instead of open-ended generation.\n\nB) UX breakthroughs for elderly / low literacy (WhatsApp-native)\nAlways offer choices\n\nUse interactive lists/buttons. \n\nOne question at a time\n\nNever ask for 3 details in one message.\n\nMulti-modal intake\n\nIf they send a photo/document:\n\nask “شو نوع المستند؟ 1 هوية 2 دفتر عائلة 3 إفادة 4 غير ذلك”\n\nError tolerance\n\n“I can’t read your message” becomes: “هل تقصد (1)… أو (2)…؟”\n\nC) Admin “teaching on the run” upgrades\nTurn your SuperAdmin Bot into a runbook + evaluator:\n\nauto-run tests:\n\n“Can we retrieve tx_fts results?”\n\n“Does WhatsApp webhook reply within X seconds?”\n\nlog failures with remediation steps\n(This aligns with agentic operations focus: governance + tooling > chat cleverness.) \n\nWhat to avoid / be careful with\n“Bot makes phone calls” and “face recognition”\nWhatsApp can’t truly initiate calls on the user’s device; you can only send tap-to-call numbers and instructions. \n\nFace recognition is a high-risk feature (privacy + legal + false positives). Keep it OFF by default; only enable if you have explicit policy + consent + a real need.\n\nConcrete upgrade checklist for your next sprint\nAdd reranker + confidence logic (top10 → best1)\n\nAdd “iterative retrieval on low confidence”\n\nConvert WhatsApp replies to interactive lis", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part59\"}"}
