nX-Hub-Signature-256 verification using WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET\n\nfeature flag: WHATSAPP_VERIFY_SIGNATURE=true|false\n\nWhy: prevents spoofed webhooks.\n\nB) Properly handle “message status” events\nWhatsApp sends delivery/read status webhooks too. Your webhook handler should:\n\nignore them cleanly\n\nnot treat them as user messages\n\nC) Idempotency (avoid double replies)\nWhatsApp can retry webhooks. Add:\n\nwa_message_id dedup table in Postgres\n\nif message_id already processed → return 200 without sending another reply\n\n2) Elderly-first UX improvements (high ROI)\nA) “Short message paging” for long responses\nAdd auto-splitting:\n\nmax ~900 chars per WhatsApp message\n\nend with: “أرسل 1 للمتابعة” (and store state: pending_next_step)\n\nB) Ultra-simple confirmations\nWhen ambiguous:\n\npresent two options only\n\n“1” and “2”, nothing else\n\nC) “Caregiver summary” mode\nIf user is in caregiver_mode:\n\nadd one short forwardable line at end: “ملخص للمتابعة: …”\n\n3) Retrieval safety & correctness\nA) Hard rule: approved-only KB\nEnsure search and chat only use:\n\nreview_status='approved'\n\nunless admin is querying\n\nB) Evidence-first response builder\nDo NOT let LLM free-write. Use KB fields:\n\ndocs, deadli", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part70\"}"}
