{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_76_watany_guide_part73", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part73", "text": "ls.\n\nWhat you should do next (so you can fully test WhatsApp + guided mode)\nAdd these to your .env (leave empty if you don’t have them yet, but Phase 3.5.1 hardening will still run):\n\nWHATSAPP_TOKEN=\nWHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=\nWHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=\n# Optional but recommended for signature verification\nWHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=\nWHATSAPP_VERIFY_SIGNATURE=false\nWhy it matters\nWithout WHATSAPP_*, your webhook router can still run locally, but you can’t:\n\nverify the webhook handshake properly (verify token)\n\nsend outbound replies through Meta\n\ndownload incoming media\n\nOne Copilot script to make the app “WhatsApp-ready” even before tokens\nThis script makes your system behave nicely in dev mode:\n\nwebhook verify endpoint works using WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN\n\nif tokens missing → app returns a clear admin warning but doesn’t crash\n\nadds a /api/admin/whatsapp/status endpoint showing what’s missing (redacted)\n\nkeeps everything safe\n\nPaste into Copilot:\n\nCOPILOT SCRIPT — WHATSAPP DEV READINESS (NO TOKENS SAFE MODE)\n\nGoal:\nMake WhatsApp integration robust in dev even when WHATSAPP_* vars are missing:\n- Don’t crash\n- Provide clear diagnostics\n- Keep webhook verify working\n- Allow unit tests to pass\n\nModify/add:\n\n1) apps/api/routers/whatsapp.py\n- On startup, read:\n WHATSAPP_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID, WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN, WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET\n- Webhook verify (GET /whatsapp/webhook):\n - if WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN missing:\n return 500 with message \"WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN not set\"\n - else proceed with handshake\n- Webhook receive (POST /whatsapp/webhook):\n - Always accept payload and process inbound text logic\n - If outbound send requires WHATSAPP_TOKEN/PHONE_NUMBER_ID and they’re missing:\n do NOT attempt to send\n instead log a warning and return 200 with {\"dev_mode\":true,\"warning\":\"WHATSAPP_TOKEN