{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_77_watany_guide_part74", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part74", "text": "d should not reply (dedup)\n\nIf you want, paste your current .env.example and I’ll rewrite it to include all WatanBot env vars (KB, Postgres, WhatsApp, OCR/STT toggles, admin flags) in a clean, production-ready template.\n\nYou said:\n\nsummarize below instructions , evaluate then rewrite as a single script to be run from within copilot vstudio window\n\nCOPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — WATANBOT “ELDERLY-FIRST” UX + WHATSAPP BUSINESS API INTEGRATION + MULTIMODAL INPUTS (SAFE, REALISTIC)\n\nRole: You are Copilot acting as a senior product engineer + backend engineer + conversation designer.\nContext:\n- WatanBot is a Lebanese veterans assistant.\n- It will be integrated with WhatsApp Business API.\n- Primary users: elderly, low digital literacy, sometimes illiterate, may use voice notes, photos, short messages, and mixed scripts.\nGoal:\n- Modify chatbot design (conversation UX + system behavior + admin settings + technical integration points) to be maximally friendly, efficient, and accessible.\n- Add support for receiving: photos, documents, location, voice notes (WhatsApp supports these).\n- Add robust input normalization: Arabic, Arabizi, Yamli-like transliteration, keyboard layout “garbled text” (Arabic typed on EN layout and vice versa).\n- IMPORTANT REALITY CHECK: WhatsApp Business API cannot actually “perform phone calls” or force actions on the user’s device. Instead:\n - Provide “action suggestions” and “tap-to-call” links or prompt text.\n - If this chatbot is embedded in a mobile app/webview in the future, those actions can become true device actions.\nImplement “action intents” that the client/WhatsApp can render as clickable actions where possible.\n\nNon-negotiable safety/accuracy:\n- No invention of procedures/fees/legal basis; answers must be grounded in KB.\n- For identity verification: do NOT do face recognition for “authentication” unless explicitly required and legally compliant.\n - If “face recognition” is requested, implement it only as an OPTIONAL feature flag, and default OFF.\n- Voice recognition: implement as a pipeline hook (WhatsApp voice note -> transcribe) with provider interface.\n - Default to “manual transcription required” if no provider keys configured.\n\n========================================================\nA) CONVERSATION DESIGN: ELDERLY-FIRST BEHAVIOR\n========================================================\nImplement a “Conversation Policy Layer” used by /api/chat and WhatsApp webhook handler.\n\nCreate module: apps/api/services/ux_policy.py\n\nRules (always):\n1) Keep responses short + structured, with 1–3 steps max per message.\n2) Always confirm intent with simple choices if user message is unclear.\n3) Use “guided mode” by default:\n - Offer buttons/numbered choices: (1) معاش تقاعد (2) طبابة (3) مدرسة/منح (4) وفاة/ورثة (5) على العاتق (6) رقم هاتف/عنوان (7) إرسال مستند\n4) Use “One question at a time”:\n - Ask only one clarifying question per turn.\n5) Use “human-friendly language” in formal Lebanese Arabic (not slang).\n6) Always provide “Wh", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part74\"}"}
