abic 101)\n- Also handle “English typed on Arabic keyboard” reverse map.\n3) Arabizi transliteration:\n- Convert common Arabizi numerals:\n 2=ء, 3=ع, 5=خ, 6=ط, 7=ح, 8=ق, 9=ص\n- Convert sh/ch/kh/gh/th/dh patterns.\n- Output candidate Arabic string.\n4) Yamli-like suggestions:\n- Produce up to 2 candidate normalized texts:\n - normalized_primary\n - normalized_alt\n5) Confidence:\n- If normalization confidence low, ask the user:\n “هل تقصد: (1) … أم (2) … ؟”\n6) Always store original_text and normalized_text in chat logs.\n\nImplement function:\nnormalize_input(text, user_lang_pref) -> {\n original, normalized, candidates[], confidence, detected_layout: \"ar_on_en\"|\"en_on_ar\"|None, detected_form: \"arabic\"|\"arabizi\"|\"mixed\"\n}\n\n========================================================\nE) CHAT ENGINE UPDATE FOR ELDERLY UX\n========================================================\nModify chat engine to:\n- Use guided mode by default:\n - If message is short (“مرحبا”, “تقاعد”, “مساعدة”), respond with menu choices.\n- When returning procedure steps:\n - Split into multiple WhatsApp messages if long (max ~800 chars each).\n - Provide “Send 1 for next step”.\n-", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part76\"}"}
