false, the chatbot will behave “plain”.\n\n3) KB content is present but NOT “approved” (or filters are too strict)\nIf your public chat filters only review_status='approved' and your KB has few approved items, you’ll get generic fallbacks.\n\n4) You’re not seeing WhatsApp “human UI” because WhatsApp interactive replies aren’t enabled/configured\nEven with the router mounted, without WhatsApp tokens + proper outbound client, you won’t see guided lists/buttons.\n\nThe fastest next move: a “Behavior Truth” test\nYou need a script that answers, with evidence:\n\nWhich endpoint the UI uses (/chat/ask vs /api/chat)\n\nWhether guided mode is ON\n\nWhether the normalizer (arabizi/garble) is running\n\nWhether reranker is being called\n\nWhether KB is returning approved results\n\nWhether WhatsApp handler can actually send messages or is in dev no-token mode\n\nCopy/paste this to Copilot (single script)\nCOPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — V3 “BEHAVIOR TRUTH” AUDIT (Why it still feels old)\n\nDo NOT write a plan. Create the audit script and the report.\n\nCreate: scripts/behavior_truth_audit.py\nCreate: docs/BEHAVIOR_TRUTH_REPORT.md\n\nThe script must:\n1) Import the real app: apps.api.main:app\n2) Print which chat endpo", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part101\"}"}
