{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_106_watany_guide_part103", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part103", "text": "STREAMLINED TEST HARNESS\n\nContext:\n- WatanBot is built for WhatsApp Business API, but WhatsApp is NOT configured yet (no tokens).\n- We must simulate WhatsApp environment end-to-end for testing: inbound webhook payloads → normalization/UX policy → chat engine/KB retrieval → outbound message payloads (without actually sending to Meta).\n- Keep everything safe: no secrets printed, no real WhatsApp network calls required.\n\nGoal:\n1) Add a “WhatsApp Simulation Mode” that:\n - Accepts sample WhatsApp webhook payloads locally\n - Runs the exact same code path as production WhatsApp handler\n - Produces the outbound WhatsApp payloads as JSON (what would be sent)\n - Stores dedup/paging/user state like real WhatsApp\n2) Add a “V3 Behavior Truth” audit and a single “one-command” test runner to streamline dev iteration.\n3) Ensure /api/chat and /chat/ask both route to the same v3 pipeline and both can return “whatsapp-style” responses when requested.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do NOT require real WhatsApp tokens.\n- Do NOT call external network APIs.\n- Do NOT break existing endpoints.\n- Do NOT invent KB facts; keep KB-grounded.\n\nFiles to add/modify:\nMODIFY:\n- apps/api/routers/whatsapp.py\n- apps/api/routers/public.py\n- apps/api/services/whatsapp_ui.py\n- apps/api/config.py\nADD:\n- apps/api/services/whatsapp_simulator.py\n- apps/api/routers/whatsapp_sim.py\n- scripts/behavior_truth_audit.py\n- scripts/whatsapp_sim_run.py\n- tests/test_whatsapp_sim.py\n- docs/WHATSAPP_SIMULATION.md\n\n========================================================\nA) CONFIG: WhatsApp simulation flags + safe defaults\n========================================================\nIn apps/api/config.py add settings:\n- WHATSAPP_SIMULATION_ENABLED (default true in dev, false in prod)\n- WHATSAPP_OUTBOUND_MODE = \"simulate\"|\"live\" (default \"simulate\" in dev)\n- WHATSAPP_INTERACTIVE_ENABLED (default true in dev)\n- STT_ENABLED (default true in dev but fallback if provider missing)\n- OCR_ENABLED (default false)\n- GUIDED_MODE_DEFAULT (default true)\n- ARABIZI_ENABLED (default true)\n- KEYBOARD_GARBLE_FIX_ENABLED (default true)\n\nAlso ensure:\n- resolve_kb_path() remains and prints missing warning only in dev.\n\n========================================================\nB) SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH CHAT PIPELINE (avoid “feels old”)\n========================================================\nIn apps/api/routers/public.py:\n- Ensure /chat/ask is the canonical handler.\n- Ensure /api/chat is a thin alias that calls the same internal function, not duplicated logic.\n- Add a request param/header to simulate channel:\n - header: X-Channel: \"web\"|\"whatsapp\"\n - OR body field: channel=\"whatsapp\"\n- When channel=\"whatsapp\", return:\n - normal ChatResponse + whatsapp_payloads[] (rendered by whatsapp_ui)\n - action_intents always included\n- Ensure both endpoints hit:\n input_normalizer → ux_policy → KB retrieval (approved only) → reranker → iterative retrieval → response builder.\n\n========================================================\nC) WHATSAPP", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part103\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_107_watany_guide_part104", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part104", "text": "ROUTER: run even without tokens (simulate send)\n========================================================\nIn apps/api/routers/whatsapp.py:\n- Keep GET/POST /whatsapp/webhook endpoints.\n- Parse inbound messages as usual.\n- Dedup using wa_dedup (if DB exists) or in-memory fallback if DB not available.\n- For outbound replies:\n - If settings.WHATSAPP_OUTBOUND_MODE == \"live\":\n call whatsapp_client.send_*\n Else (\"simulate\"):\n DO NOT call network. Instead:\n - build outbound payload(s) using whatsapp_ui\n - return 200 JSON:\n {\n \"mode\":\"simulate\",\n \"to\": \"<phone>\",\n \"outbound\": [<payload1>, <payload2>...],\n \"debug\": {\"normalized\":..., \"guided\":..., \"paging\":...}\n }\n- This makes webhook testable without Meta.\n\nAlso handle:\n- statuses-only events: ignore and return 200\n- voice note: if STT provider missing, ask for keywords; do not fail\n- media/doc: ask doc type 1/2/3/4 if OCR off\n- location: store and ask 1/2/3\n\n========================================================\nD) WHATSAPP SIMULATOR SERVICE (core of dev testing)\n========================================================\nCreate apps/api/services/whatsapp_simulator.py:\n- build_sample_payload_text(phone, text)\n- build_sample_payload_voice(phone, media_id=\"SIM_AUDIO_1\")\n- build_sample_payload_image(phone, media_id=\"SIM_IMG_1\")\n- build_sample_payload_document(phone, media_id=\"SIM_DOC_1\")\n- build_sample_payload_location(phone, lat, lng, address=None)\n- Each payload must match WhatsApp Cloud API webhook structure closely.\n\n- simulate_inbound(app, payload):\n - internally call the same handler function used by POST /whatsapp/webhook\n - return the outbound simulated payload JSON\n\n========================================================\nE) WHATSAPP SIM ROUTER (developer convenience)\n========================================================\nCreate apps/api/routers/whatsapp_sim.py and mount it in apps/api/main.py (dev only):\nEndpoints:\n- POST /dev/whatsapp/simulate (accepts {phone, type, text?, lat?, lng?})\n - Builds payload and runs simulation\n- GET /dev/whatsapp/samples (returns ready-to-copy JSON examples)\n- POST /dev/whatsapp/replay (accepts raw webhook payload and runs simulation)\n\nSecurity:\n- Only enabled if APP_ENV=dev AND WHATSAPP_SIMULATION_ENABLED=true\n\n========================================================\nF) WHATSAPP UI: make outputs “human”\n========================================================\nUpdate apps/api/services/whatsapp_ui.py:\n- split_text(message, max_len=900)\n- build_list_menu(title, items) (max 7)\n- build_reply_buttons(text, buttons) (max 3)\n- render_action_intents(intents):\n - call_phone -> show number + “اضغط للاتصال”\n - open_url -> show URL\n - request_location/photo/voice -> clear instruction + button if possible\n- Provide fallback: numbered options when interactive disabled\n\n========================================================\nG) V3 BEHAVIOR TRUTH AUDIT (updated for WhatsApp simulation)\n==============", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part104\"}"}
