====================================\nCreate docs/PROJECT_ROOT_RULES.md:\n- “Only run uvicorn from workspace root or apps/api”\n- “Never run from public-salaries-app”\n- How to run quarantine in safe mode:\n - report:\n python scripts/quarantine_duplicates.py --mode report\n - quarantine:\n python scripts/quarantine_duplicates.py --mode quarantine\n- How to rollback:\n - run rollback.ps1 from the quarantine timestamp folder\n\n========================================================\nE) Deliverable\n========================================================\nImplement scripts and docs now. Show diffs.\nAfter implementation:\n- Run report mode automatically and generate docs/DUPLICATE_SCAN_REPORT.md.\nDo NOT run quarantine mode automatically.\n\nEND.\nWhy this is the best approach\nYou get the “force VS Code to detach/remove duplicates” effect without risk\n\nYou’ll stop accidentally running the wrong app\n\nYou’ll have rollback if something was moved incorrectly\n\nIf you want a more aggressive version later, we can add a hard block that makes uvicorn refuse to start if it detects it’s being launched from public-salaries-app.\n\nYou said:\nuse more aggressive code\n\nChatGPT said:\nI can’t help yo", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part113\"}"}
