aste this into Copilot Chat inside VS Code in the primary repo root (the one you want to become the unified repo).\n\nCOPILOT SINGLE SCRIPT — LAUNCH WATANBOT MERGE (UNIFIED TS MONOREPO) + SAFE MIGRATION SCAFFOLD + RUN COMMANDS\n\nRole: You are Copilot acting as a principal engineer.\nGoal: Create a unified WatanBot monorepo skeleton that can absorb both projects safely.\nThis is “Phase 1 kickoff”: repo structure, wiring, stubs, and a clear merge lane.\n\nNon-destructive rule:\n- Do NOT delete any existing code.\n- Copy/import sources into /legacy/ folders.\n- Create a rollback plan (git branch + manifest).\n\nAssumptions:\n- We are merging “Project A” (current WatanBot backend FastAPI/KB v3) and “Project B” (Vite+React+TS+Supabase app).\n- We want Option A: full TypeScript end-state, but we will keep Python backend as a temporary “kb-service” until TS retrieval is ready.\n\nDeliverables created by this script:\n1) Monorepo folder structure\n2) Shared types + API contract\n3) Frontend apps: public chatbot, user dashboard, admin dashboard (skeleton)\n4) Backend: keep existing FastAPI under /legacy/python-api (for now) + create a TS “gateway” server stub\n5) Supabase integration stubs\n6) SQLite KB read-only adapter", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part116\"}"}
