e and adaptable as possible to your immediate question. I didn’t mean to revert unintentionally. Now that we’re clear—let’s stick to that military focus for you! What’s the next specific thing you’d like me to help with in that area?\n\nYou said:\n“How about you walk me through how to set you up in a way where your answers and your specialization is consistent and you don't keep going back to the default of being a generalized AI.”\n00:11\n\nChatGPT said:\nWe can definitely avoid those shifts by using a system that remembers context. If we integrate into a platform where user preferences or session goals are stored—like a dedicated app or a chatbot with memory—that ensures I stick to your chosen role. Right now, I’m flexible by design, but if we build or use a system with saved settings, I’d consistently know: \"I’m the retired military specialist!\" Until then, just remind me if I drift, and I’ll snap right back into focus. Sound like a plan?\n\nYou said:\nProceed with app building \n\nChatGPT said:\nAlright — let’s proceed and start building the WatanBot app in a way that keeps the role consistent:\n\nWatanBot is NOT a generic chatbot.\nIt is built to help", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part216\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_220_watany_guide_part217", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part217", "text": "retired Lebanese military personnel and their families (wife/husband, children, parents of martyr, etc.) with pensions, compensations, healthcare, schooling support, required documents, where to apply, and follow-up workflows.\nFor anything outside that scope, it can optionally answer “citizen-level” questions using general AI — but only as a secondary path.\n\nBelow is a clean MVP build you can run on Windows (and later deploy on your server). It includes the flag/ticket workflow you asked for.\n\n1) What we’re building (MVP v1)\nUser App (Chat)\nChat UI (Arabic-friendly)\n\n“Step-by-step” answers (not dumping everything)\n\nAlways ends with:\n\n“Do you want where to apply, required documents, or eligibility?”\n\nthen a satisfaction question\n\nIf user is unhappy → create a ticket automatically\n\nKnowledge Sources (priority rule you set)\nAnswer priority:\n\nLaws / decrees / official circulars\n\nMinistry of Finance PDFs + forms (MoF pensioners pages)\n\nThe “guide” you uploaded is supporting / structuring questions, not the source of truth\n\nAdmin Console\nReview flagged answers\n\nClose ticket after fixing KB entry\n\nUpdate KB and mark correction\n\n2) Tech stack (simple + solid)\nBackend: FastAPI (Python)\n\nDB: SQLite (for MVP) → can later switch to Postgres\n\nFrontend: React (Vite)\n\nSearch: SQLite FTS (fast text search) + metadata filters\n\nFiles: store PDFs locally + link them\n\n3) Folder structure\nCreate a folder like:\n\nwatanbot/\n backend/\n frontend/\n data/\n kb/\n files/\n scripts/\n4) Database schema (includes tickets + satisfaction)\nCreate backend/app/db/schema.sql:\n\n-- Knowledge items (the “cards”)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS kb_items (\n id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n title TEXT NOT NULL,\n scope TEXT NOT NULL, -- \"retired_military\" etc\n topic TEXT NOT NULL, -- \"pension\", \"reallocation\", \"dependents\", ...\n summary TEXT,\n answer_steps TEXT, -- JSON string: step-by-step answer chunks\n where_to_apply TEXT, -- JSON string\n required_documents TEXT, -- JSON string\n eligibility TEXT, -- JSON string\n citations TEXT, -- JSON string (law/article/pdf/page/url)\n updated_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Full-text search for kb_items\nCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS kb_fts USING fts5(\n id, title, topic, summary, content\n);\n\n-- Tickets created when user says answer is wrong / unsatisfied\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tickets (\n id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n status TEXT NOT NULL, -- open|in_review|fixed|closed\n user_session_id TEXT,\n user_question TEXT,\n bot_answer TEXT,\n user_feedback TEXT,\n suspected_issue TEXT, -- \"wrong authority\", \"missing condition\", etc\n kb_item_id TEXT,\n admin_notes TEXT\n);\n\n-- Chat sessions (optional but useful)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (\n id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n last_seen_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Message logs (optional)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (\n id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part217\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_221_watany_guide_part218", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part218", "text": "session_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n role TEXT NOT NULL, -- user|bot\n text TEXT NOT NULL,\n created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n5) Backend (FastAPI) — minimal but complete\nbackend/app/main.py\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\nfrom app.routes.chat import router as chat_router\nfrom app.routes.admin import router as admin_router\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"WatanBot API\", version=\"0.1\")\n\napp.add_middleware(\n CORSMiddleware,\n allow_origins=[\"http://localhost:5173\"],\n allow_credentials=True,\n allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n allow_headers=[\"*\"],\n)\n\napp.include_router(chat_router, prefix=\"/api\")\napp.include_router(admin_router, prefix=\"/api/admin\")\nbackend/app/db/db.py\nimport sqlite3\n see\n::contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}\n(continuing — and keeping it implementable, not overwhelming)\n\nbackend/app/db/db.py\nimport sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDB_PATH = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"watanbot.db\"\n\ndef get_conn():\n conn = sqlite3.connect(DB_PATH)\n conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n return conn\nbackend/app/db/init_db.py\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom app.db.db import get_conn\n\nSCHEMA_PATH = Path(__file__).parent / \"schema.sql\"\n\ndef main():\n schema = SCHEMA_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n conn = get_conn()\n try:\n conn.executescript(schema)\n conn.commit()\n print(f\"DB initialized at: {conn.execute('PRAGMA database_list').fetchone()[2]}\")\n finally:\n conn.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n main()\n6) Chat logic (your “step-by-step + confirm + satisfaction + ticket” rule)\nbackend/app/routes/chat.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport json, uuid\n\nfrom app.db.db import get_conn\n\nrouter = APIRouter()\n\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\n session_id: str | None = None\n message: str\n\nclass ChatResponse(BaseModel):\n session_id: str\n mode: str # \"kb\" | \"handoff\" | \"out_of_scope\"\n reply: str\n suggestions: list[str] = []\n\ndef now():\n return datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n\nSYSTEM_SCOPE_NOTE = (\n \"أنا مساعد مخصص للعسكريين المتقاعدين وعائلاتهم: \"\n \"معاشات، تعويضات، طبابة، مساعدات مدرسية، معاملات وزارة المالية/الدفاع، والمستندات المطلوبة.\"\n)\n\n@router.post(\"/chat\", response_model=ChatResponse)\ndef chat(req: ChatRequest):\n session_id = req.session_id or str(uuid.uuid4())\n user_text = (req.message or \"\").strip()\n\n # Save session + message\n conn = get_conn()\n try:\n conn.execute(\n \"INSERT OR IGNORE INTO sessions(id, created_at, last_seen_at) VALUES(?,?,?)\",\n (session_id, now(), now()),\n )\n conn.execute(\"UPDATE sessions SET last_seen_at=? WHERE id=?\", (now(), session_id))\n conn.execute(\n \"INSERT INTO messages(id, session_id, role, text, created_at) VALUES(?,?,?,?,?)\",\n (str(uuid.uuid4()), session_id, \"user\", user_text, now()),\n )\n conn.commit()\n\n # Search KB (FTS)", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part218\"}"}
