t to implement first: (1), (2), or (3)?\n\nYou said:\nProceed with all three in sequence , at the end I need a fully detailed script produced by the lead consultant software engineer to produce for handout for the dleoftware design and programming engineer tasked to develop the app\n\nThe script will be used to generate full building automation otlf the app with vs code and copilot and docker to develop the app\n\nChatGPT said:\nGot it. Below is a lead-software-engineer handoff script that your dev can use with VS Code + Copilot + Docker to build the app end-to-end, implementing (1) MoF KB import, then (2) ticketing + admin UI, then (3) voice notes + guided flows — in that exact sequence.\n\nThis is written as a build-automation + engineering spec: your programmer can literally follow it, copy/paste the commands, and scaffold the whole repo.\n\nWatanBot Build Handoff Script\nProject: WatanBot (Retired Military & Families Assistant)\nPrimary Scope: pensions, compensations, healthcare, schooling support, dependents, required documents, where-to-apply, follow-up workflows.\nTruth-source priority rule (MANDATORY):\n\nLaws / decrees / official circulars\n\nMinistry of Finance PDFs + forms + official pages\n\n“Guide", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part221\"}"}
