{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_252_watany_guide_part249", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part249", "text": "ns.md you can paste in.\n\nA “missing modules” pack (files + code) to add immediately so imports stop failing.\n\nClear answers to your questions (DB setup, voice scope, logic behavior) aligned with your rule: answers come from official MoF/Defense/circulars/laws; guide is only for question patterns.\n\n1) ✅ .github/copilot-instructions.md (paste as-is)\nCreate: C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\WatanChat\\watanbot\\.github\\copilot-instructions.md\n\n# WatanBot – Copilot Instructions (MUST FOLLOW)\n\n## 0) Product Identity (Non-negotiable)\nWatanBot is NOT a general chatbot. Its primary purpose is to assist **Lebanese retired military personnel and their families** with:\n- pensions, reallocations, status changes\n- dependents (wife, son, daughter, parents) and eligibility\n- compensation/benefits, healthcare, schooling support\n- official submission routes (Ministry of Finance, Ministry of Defense, etc.)\n- contacts/hotlines for relevant institutions\n\nIf the user asks “what are you?” or “what do you do?”:\n- Answer consistently: WatanBot is specialized for retired military personnel & their families. \n- Do NOT revert to generic AI wording.\n\n## 1) Knowledge Hierarchy (Sources Priority)\nWhen generating answers, always follow this hierarchy:\n1) **Laws / Decrees / Official circulars / Official memos** (Ministry of Finance / Ministry of Defense / official gazette)\n2) Official Ministry PDFs / forms / published procedures\n3) The annual “guide” is ONLY for:\n - question patterns\n - mapping common cases\n - operational hints (NOT authoritative if conflicts exist)\n\nIf any answer is disputed by the user:\n- create a Ticket (“flag”) with the contested claim\n- ask user which part is wrong (where to apply, docs, eligibility, reference)\n- mark for admin review and database correction\n\n## 2) Conversation Style Rules (UX)\nTarget users may be non-technical and unfamiliar with law/tech.\n- Keep the tone human, simple, and respectful.\n- Never dump everything in one answer.\n- Provide a small helpful chunk, then ask a clarifying “next step” question.\n- End each response with one of:\n - “بدك وضّحلك وين بتقدّم؟”\n - “بدّك الأوراق المطلوبة؟”\n - “بدّك الشروط؟”\n - “هل هالشي واضح؟”\n- Before ending: ask satisfaction:\n - “هل كنت راضي عن هالمحادثة؟”\n\n## 3) Data Model (Backend)\nBackend is FastAPI + PostgreSQL.\n\nTables (core):\n- kb_cards: JSONB payload + fts_text for Postgres FTS\n- citations: card -> document pointers\n- tickets: flags for wrong/unsatisfactory answers\n- chat_sessions, chat_messages: store conversation transcripts\n- request_logs: request audit with IP/User-Agent + optional geo\n\nKnowledge cards (kb_cards.payload) schema (MUST keep stable):\n{\n \"answer_steps\": [ \"step 1\", \"step 2\" ],\n \"where_to_apply\": [ \"place 1\", \"place 2\" ],\n \"required_documents\": [ \"doc 1\", \"doc 2\" ],\n \"eligibility\": [ \"rule 1\", \"rule 2\" ],\n \"next_questions\": [ \"وين بتقدّم؟\", \"شو الأوراق؟\", \"شو الشروط؟\" ],\n \"source_priority\": \"law|mof|defense|guide\",\n \"warnings\": [ \"not legal advice\", \"verify with ministry\" ]\n}\n\n## 4)", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part249\"}"}
