ause it directly serves low-literacy users.\n\nTTS later (text → voice) is easy once you have stable answer text.\n\nVoice fingerprinting is not MVP: it requires biometric design, consent, storage policy, and a real pipeline. Keep it “future” and do not fake it.\n\nQ4) “Business logic behaviors?”\nFor now:\n\nminimal_step_answer() must not dump everything.\n\nclassify_issue() must categorize complaints into a small set:\n\nreference / where-to-apply / documents / eligibility / other\n\nAdd “ask next” behavior at the end of each answer.\n\nThis matches exactly what you demanded: structured conversation in steps + ticket flagging.\n\nWhat to do next (exact steps)\nAdd the files above (5 stubs).\n\nRebuild:\n\ndocker compose up -d --build\n\nTest:\n\nhttp://localhost:8000/api/health\n\nTry chat endpoint and confirm it returns:\n\nscope note + small answer + next question prompt.\n\nIf you want, paste your current backend/app/ tree and I’ll give you a single “patch script” that creates these files automatically (so you don’t copy/paste manually).\n\nYou said:\ngive me a single script to insert into copilot window\n\nChatGPT said:\nBelow is one single “Cop", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part251\"}"}
