t the UI must call)\nUser window needs these endpoint capabilities (even if you implement later):\n\nsearch transactions (FTS)\n\nget transaction detail\n\nsearch law articles\n\nget law article detail\n\nget tx ↔ law mapping\n\nget related procedures\n\nsalary lookup (rank+degree)\n\nsave/bookmark (auth)\n\ncase CRUD (auth)\n\nfeedback/report (public/auth)\n\nIf you want, I’ll now turn this exact list into a single Copilot-ready implementation script plan (frontend components + backend endpoints + DB schema bindings) in the stack you chose earlier (Vite/React/TS + Supabase OR FastAPI + SQLite).\n\nYou said:\nfrom now on dont use municipality with chatbot , produce script that combine all previous discussions reagrding coding a full feature user window\n\nChatGPT said:\nUpdated saved memory\n\nThought for 8s\nGot it — no municipality features anywhere in the chatbot going forward.\n\nBelow is one single script you can run in VS Code terminal (PowerShell on Windows) that scaffolds a full-feature user window for Watany (retired military chatbot) using:\n\nVite + React + TypeScript\n\nRTL Arabic UI (default) + EN/FR switch\n\nArabizi detection + normalization for search\n\nChat window + citations toggle\n\nKB Search + Browse by Sections\n\nSalar", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part304\"}"}
