{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_411_watany_guide_part408", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part408", "text": "personnel and their families (pensions, compensations, healthcare, schools, administrative requests).\n\nKnowledge base and mapping\nConvert the retirees’ administrative/financial guide into a structured KB (procedures “معاملة رقم X”).\n\nMap each procedure to its legal basis, starting with:\n\nNational Defense Law\n\nthen Labor Law\n\nand Lebanese Civil Servants/Employees Law\n\nBuild and store procedure correlations (related transactions, dependency links like death → inheritance → pension transfer).\n\nSalaries and tables\nExtract salary data from salary scale tables (سلسلة رتب ورواتب).\n\nProvide salary lookup by:\n\nrank + degree\n\nand ability to answer examples like: “عميد درجة رابعة” based on the tables.\n\nRetrieval and search\nUse SQLite KB as the authoritative store.\n\nAdd FTS (full-text search) for fast Arabic search across:\n\nprocedures\n\nlegal articles\n\nsalaries tables\n\nProduce RAG-ready JSONL chunks for embedding/retrieval.\n\nApp structure (three-part system)\nPublic chatbot (no auth): general questions, guidance, eligibility checks, what documents needed.\n\nUser dashboard (auth): saved conversations, bookmarks, saved procedures, personal case tracking.\n\nAdmin dashboard (auth): manage KB (add/edit procedures, laws, salary tables), approve mappings, view analytics.\n\nPermissions and security\nAuthentication + role-based permissions\n\npublic user\n\nauthenticated retiree/family user\n\nadmin/editor\n\nKeep answers non-personalized unless authenticated (no “your exact salary” unless the app later has secured user records).\n\nAnalytics and ops\nBasic analytics:\n\nmost asked questions\n\nmost referenced procedures\n\nfailure / no-answer logs\n\nsearch terms trends\n\nImport/export tools:\n\nexport CSV/JSONL\n\nre-ingest updated docs\n\nversioning (KB v1/v2/v3)\n\nNice-to-have (conditional)\nGIS/municipality features were discussed elsewhere, but for this chatbot they’re not required unless tied directly to retired-military services.\n\nIf you want, I can turn this list into a backlog (MVP vs Phase 2 vs Phase 3) so you can build in VS Code with Copilot in the right order.\n\nYou said:\nkeep teh above mentioned modifications, but i need you to state also every tiny detail regarding the functionality of the window on the user side , like at least we asked for arabizi, yet it was not mentioned in your summary , therefore remap all discussions and look closely for funtions discussed pertaining th=o the user windo relist here so we acn perapare a script for implemntation\n\nChatGPT said:\n\nThought for 47s\nBelow is the full remap of user-side “chatbot window” functionality we’ve discussed across the Watany/WatanBot work (public chatbot + user dashboard), including the missing Arabizi requirement, and every small UX behavior that matters for implementation.\n\nI’m keeping everything from the previous summary (KB, laws mapping, salaries, search, 3-part system, permissions, analytics) and expanding the user window details.\n\nA) User-side window modes and navigation\n1) Two user entry modes\nPublic Chat (no login)\n\nCa", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part408\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_412_watany_guide_part409", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part409", "text": "n ask questions, search KB, view procedures, view legal basis excerpts.\n\nCannot access any personal profile/salary record. Only table-based/official/public outputs.\n\nLogged-in User Dashboard\n\nEverything in public + personal features: saved cases, bookmarks, history, file vault, reminders.\n\n2) Global navigation in the chat window\nTop bar includes:\n\nWatany logo + title\n\nLanguage selector (Arabic default + English + French)\n\nRTL/LTR auto-switch based on selected language\n\nLogin/Profile button\n\nHelp / “How it works”\n\nFeedback/Report issue\n\n3) Left panel (optional) / drawer menu\nBrowse KB (sections + transactions list)\n\nSalaries lookup\n\nSaved / Bookmarks\n\nMy Cases (auth only)\n\nDownloads/Exports\n\nSettings (language, display, citations toggle)\n\nB) Language, writing style, and Arabizi support (important)\n1) Language behavior\nArabic is default, with formal Lebanese-friendly Arabic (not street talk).\n\nUser can switch to English/French anytime.\n\nMixed-language messages are allowed; the system should:\n\ndetect dominant language,\n\nanswer in the currently selected UI language,\n\npreserve any legal terms in Arabic if necessary.\n\n2) Arabizi support (requested)\nUser may type Arabic using Latin letters + numbers (Arabizi), e.g.:\n\n“3amīd daraje rabe3a” / “3amīd 4”\n\n“2ab”, “7a2”, “5edme”, etc.\n\nRequired functionality:\n\nDetect Arabizi automatically (pattern: Latin letters + digits 2/3/5/7/8/9).\n\nConvert Arabizi → Arabic (transliteration) for search + retrieval only.\n\nKeep both in memory:\n\nuser_raw_input (original)\n\nnormalized_input_ar (converted)\n\nDisplay behavior:\n\nAnswer in the chosen UI language\n\nOptionally show a small line: “تم فهم طلبك كالتالي: …” (toggleable)\n\nC) Chat input and message composer behavior\n1) Input box features\nPlaceholder guidance (contextual):\n\n“اسأل عن معاملة… مثل: ضمان الوالدين، وفاة، حصر إرث…”\n\nSend:\n\nEnter = send\n\nShift+Enter = new line\n\nButtons:\n\nAttach file (PDF/photo/doc)\n\nVoice input (optional)\n\nClear chat\n\n2) User intent shortcuts (chips)\nUnder the input or above the chat:\n\n“📌 معاملات”\n\n“💰 رواتب”\n\n“⚕️ طبابة”\n\n“🎓 مدارس”\n\n“👨‍👩‍👧‍👦 عائلة / على العاتق”\n\n“⚖️ أساس قانوني”\n\n“📍 أين أقدّم الطلب؟”\n\n“📄 المستندات المطلوبة”\n\nClicking a chip should:\n\nPre-fill query\n\nOr open a mini form (salary lookup, dependent eligibility, etc.)\n\nD) Answer formatting (what the user sees)\nEvery answer (when relevant) should be structured into consistent blocks:\n\n1) “Result summary” block\n2–4 lines: what the user needs + outcome.\n\n2) “Eligibility / Conditions” block\nBullet rules, age conditions, dependency rules (if present in guide).\n\n3) “Required documents” block\nChecklist format ✅\n\nWith repeated docs normalized (e.g., “إخراج قيد” appears once with notes)\n\n4) “Steps / Workflow” block\nStep-by-step flow\n\n“Where to submit” + “Which office”\n\n5) “Fees / amounts / time limits” block\nIf text includes fees or deadlines: show clearly.\n\n6) “Legal basis” block (mapped laws)\nShow:\n\nLaw name\n\nArticle number(s)\n\nShort excerpt/summary\n\nMust include a “View full article” action that", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part409\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_413_watany_guide_part410", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part410", "text": "opens the article panel.\n\n7) “Related procedures” block (correlations)\nShow “You may also need…” with 3–5 related transactions.\n\nThese come from the correlations graph we built (tx_links / similarity).\n\n8) “Sources & citations” behavior\nToggle: “Show sources”\n\nIf ON: show links like:\n\n“الدليل – المعاملة رقم X”\n\n“قانون الدفاع الوطني – المادة Y”\n\n(Optional) show PDF page references if available.\n\nE) Search & browse behavior (user experience)\n1) Two search modes inside the same window\nAsk Watany (chat): natural language Q/A\n\nSearch KB (direct): returns matching transactions/law articles like a search engine\n\n2) Search results cards (transactions)\nEach card shows:\n\nTransaction number + title\n\nSection name\n\nShort preview\n\nButtons:\n\nOpen details\n\nSave/Bookmark\n\nRelated procedures\n\n3) Browse by sections (accordion)\nSection list (القسم الأول…)\n\nExpand shows all “معاملة رقم …”\n\nClicking opens the transaction detail view (not just chat)\n\nF) Salary lookup UI (tables-based)\nWe discussed salary extraction by rank + degree from salary tables.\n\n1) Salary Lookup mini-form\nDropdown: Rank\n\nInput/Dropdown: Degree\n\nOptional: Year (e.g., 2017 if the table is year-specific)\n\nOutput:\n\nbase salary / new salary / allowances columns (as per extracted table fields)\n\nAction buttons:\n\nCopy result\n\nExport row\n\nShow source table (table # / page)\n\n2) Salary answers must be table-based\nIf user says: “عميد درجة رابعة”:\n\nbot uses normalized table mapping and outputs the row values.\n\nMust clearly say “وفق جدول …” (source).\n\nG) “My Account” features (logged-in user dashboard)\n1) Saved items\nBookmarks:\n\ntransactions\n\nlaw articles\n\nsalary results\n\nTags and notes on saved items\n\n2) Conversation history\nSearch inside history\n\nRename a conversation\n\nExport chat transcript (PDF/HTML)\n\n3) Case tracking (requested direction)\nCreate a “Case”:\n\ntype (death/inheritance, dependent, schooling, medical, pension payment)\n\nstatus checklist\n\nrequired docs checklist\n\nAttach documents to a case (private vault)\n\nReminders (optional automation): “remind me to renew docs / submit”\n\nH) Trust, privacy, and guardrails in the user window\n1) Privacy disclaimers\nAlways visible in small text or in help:\n\nThe bot provides guidance; not official legal advice\n\nPersonal salary/pension amounts require official authenticated systems (unless table-based)\n\n2) No personal exposure by default\nPublic users: never output “your salary”, only “table-based”\n\nAuth users: still only show what is inside KB unless you later integrate secure user payroll APIs.\n\n3) Feedback loop\n“This answer helped / didn’t help”\n\n“Report incorrect mapping” (stores a flag for admin review)\n\nI) Admin-driven but user-visible outcomes\nEven though admin tools are separate, the user window depends on:\n\nVersioned KB (v1/v2/v3)\n\n“Last updated” label per transaction\n\nMapping improvements reflected immediately\n\n“Suggested correction received” acknowledgment\n\nJ) Implementation hooks (what the UI must call)\nUser window needs these endpoint capabilities (even", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part410\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_414_watany_guide_part411", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part411", "text": "if you implement later):\n\nsearch transactions (FTS)\n\nget transaction detail\n\nsearch law articles\n\nget law article detail\n\nget tx ↔ law mapping\n\nget related procedures\n\nsalary lookup (rank+degree)\n\nsave/bookmark (auth)\n\ncase CRUD (auth)\n\nfeedback/report (public/auth)\n\nIf you want, I’ll now turn this exact list into a single Copilot-ready implementation script plan (frontend components + backend endpoints + DB schema bindings) in the stack you chose earlier (Vite/React/TS + Supabase OR FastAPI + SQLite).\n\nYou said:\nfrom now on dont use municipality with chatbot , produce script that combine all previous discussions reagrding coding a full feature user window\n\nChatGPT said:\nUpdated saved memory\n\nThought for 8s\nGot it — no municipality features anywhere in the chatbot going forward.\n\nBelow is one single script you can run in VS Code terminal (PowerShell on Windows) that scaffolds a full-feature user window for Watany (retired military chatbot) using:\n\nVite + React + TypeScript\n\nRTL Arabic UI (default) + EN/FR switch\n\nArabizi detection + normalization for search\n\nChat window + citations toggle\n\nKB Search + Browse by Sections\n\nSalary lookup (rank + degree) UI\n\nBookmarks + History\n\nMy Cases (basic tracking)\n\nFeedback/report answer\n\nMock API layer now (so UI works), easy to swap to your real SQLite/KB API later\n\nRun this once, it creates all files.\n\n# watany_user_window_full.ps1\n# One-shot scaffold for Watany Retired Military Chatbot - User Window (NO municipality features)\n# Creates: Vite React TS app + full UI + mock API + Arabizi support\n\nparam(\n [string]$AppName = \"watany-user-window\",\n [int]$Port = 5173\n)\n\n$ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\"\nfunction Info($m){Write-Host \"[INFO] $m\" -ForegroundColor Cyan}\nfunction Ok($m){Write-Host \"[ OK ] $m\" -ForegroundColor Green}\n\nInfo \"Creating app: $AppName\"\nif (!(Get-Command node -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) { throw \"Node.js not found. Install Node 18+.\" }\nif (Test-Path $AppName) { throw \"Folder '$AppName' already exists.\" }\n\n# 1) Create Vite React TS app\nnpm create vite@latest $AppName -- --template react-ts | Out-Null\nSet-Location $AppName\n\nInfo \"Installing deps...\"\nnpm install | Out-Null\n\n# 2) Add lightweight deps (no shadcn required for this scaffold)\nnpm install clsx | Out-Null\n\n# 3) Write files\nInfo \"Writing source files...\"\n\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path \"src\\app\",\"src\\components\",\"src\\lib\",\"src\\pages\",\"src\\store\",\"src\\types\" | Out-Null\n\n@\"\nexport type Lang = \"ar\" | \"en\" | \"fr\";\n\nexport type Citation = {\n kind: \"guide_tx\" | \"law_article\" | \"salary_table\";\n label: string;\n ref?: string; // e.g. \"tx_12\" or \"NDL_94\" or \"table_18_row_4\"\n};\n\nexport type ChatRole = \"user\" | \"assistant\" | \"system\";\n\nexport type ChatMessage = {\n id: string;\n role: ChatRole;\n ts: number;\n text: string;\n citations?: Citation[];\n meta?: Record<string, any>;\n};\n\nexport type TxItem = {\n tx_no: number;\n title_ar: string;\n section_ar: string;\n preview: string;\n};\n\nexport type TxDetail = TxItem & {\n body:", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part411\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_415_watany_guide_part412", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part412", "text": "string;\n required_docs?: string[];\n steps?: string[];\n fees_lbp?: number[];\n time_limits?: string[];\n phones?: string[];\n urls?: string[];\n related?: { tx_no: number; title_ar: string; similarity: number }[];\n legal_basis?: { law: string; article_no: number; excerpt: string }[];\n};\n\nexport type SalaryResult = {\n rank_ar: string;\n degree: number;\n new_salary_lbp?: number;\n base_salary_old_lbp?: number;\n cola_lbp?: number;\n notes?: string;\n source?: Citation;\n};\n\nexport type CaseItem = {\n id: string;\n title: string;\n type: \"dependents\" | \"death_inheritance\" | \"medical\" | \"schooling\" | \"pension_payment\" | \"other\";\n status: \"draft\" | \"in_progress\" | \"submitted\" | \"done\";\n checklist: { label: string; done: boolean }[];\n createdAt: number;\n updatedAt: number;\n};\n\nexport type UserProfile = {\n isAuthed: boolean;\n name?: string;\n};\n\"@ | Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 \"src\\types\\domain.ts\"\n\n@\"\nimport { clsx } from \"clsx\";\nexport function cn(...args: any[]) { return clsx(args); }\n\nexport function uid(prefix=\"id\") {\n return `${prefix}_${Math.random().toString(16).slice(2)}_${Date.now().toString(16)}`;\n}\n\"@ | Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 \"src\\lib\\utils.ts\"\n\n@\"\nimport type { Lang } from \"../types/domain\";\n\nconst ARABIZI_DIGITS: Record<string,string> = {\n \"2\":\"أ\", \"3\":\"ع\", \"5\":\"خ\", \"6\":\"ط\", \"7\":\"ح\", \"8\":\"ق\", \"9\":\"ص\"\n};\n\n/**\n * Minimal Arabizi detection + normalization for SEARCH (not for display).\n * - Detects Latin letters mixed with 2/3/5/6/7/8/9.\n * - Outputs an Arabic-ish string to help KB retrieval.\n */\nexport function isProbablyArabizi(s: string): boolean {\n const hasLatin = /[a-z]/i.test(s);\n const hasArabiziNums = /[2356789]/.test(s);\n const hasArabic = /[\\u0600-\\u06FF]/.test(s);\n return hasLatin && hasArabiziNums && !hasArabic;\n}\n\nexport function arabiziToArabicForSearch(input: string): string {\n let s = (input || \"\").toLowerCase();\n // common digraphs\n s = s.replace(/kh/g, \"خ\").replace(/gh/g, \"غ\").replace(/sh/g, \"ش\").replace(/ch/g, \"تش\");\n s = s.replace(/th/g, \"ث\").replace(/dh/g, \"ذ\");\n // numbers\n s = s.replace(/[2356789]/g, (m) => ARABIZI_DIGITS[m] || m);\n // crude phonetic replacements\n s = s.replace(/aa|a/g, \"ا\")\n .replace(/ee|i/g, \"ي\")\n .replace(/oo|u/g, \"و\");\n // remove leftover latin\n s = s.replace(/[a-z]/g, \" \");\n // cleanup\n s = s.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n return s;\n}\n\nexport function dirForLang(lang: Lang) {\n return lang === \"ar\" ? \"rtl\" : \"ltr\";\n}\n\"@ | Set-Content -Encoding UTF8 \"src\\lib\\lang.ts\"\n\n@\"\nimport type { CaseItem, ChatMessage, Lang, SalaryResult, TxDetail, TxItem, UserProfile } from \"../types/domain\";\nimport { uid } from \"./utils\";\n\n/**\n * MOCK API for UI development.\n * Replace these with real endpoints later:\n * - /api/search/tx?q=\n * - /api/tx/:tx_no\n * - /api/salary?rank=&degree=\n * - /api/cases CRUD\n */\n\nconst MOCK_TX: TxItem[] = [\n { tx_no: 12, title_ar: \"إضافة الزوجة على العاتق\", section_ar: \"الشؤون المالية\", preview: \"شروط إضافة الزوجة على العاتق والمستندات المطلوبة...", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part412\"}"}
