ings\n\nResolves relative paths against the index location\n\nCrawls each linked local file (HTML first; PDFs/DOCX optional)\n\nExtracts readable text\n\nDetects “Required documents” patterns and attaches them to the correct form entry\n\nOutputs:\n\nkb/forms.json\n\nkb/chunks.jsonl (for embeddings/RAG)\n\nkb/link_map.csv (audit / debugging)\n\n4) Starter “one-script” implementation (Node.js) — ready for VSCode/Copilot\nBelow is a practical scaffold that will work once you run it inside your project (and after you upload/share the folder structure). It does mapping + HTML text extraction. Then you can extend PDF/DOCX extraction.\n\n// build_kb.js\n// Usage: node build_kb.js \"C:/Users/User/watanbot/mofdoc/index.html\"\n\nimport fs from \"fs\";\nimport path from \"path\";\nimport { JSDOM } from \"jsdom\";\n\nfunction readFileSafe(p) {\n return fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\");\n}\n\nfunction normalize(p) {\n return p.replace(/\\\\/g, \"/\");\n}\n\nfunction resolveHref(indexPath, href) {\n // ignore external, mailto, tel, javascript\n if (!href) return null;\n if (/^(https?:)?\\/\\//i.test(href)) return null;\n if (/^(mailto:|tel:|javascript:)/i.test(href)) return null;\n\n const baseDir = path.dirname(indexPath);\n const cleanHref = href.split(\"#\")[0].split(\"?\")[0];\n\n // handle absolute-like /path insi", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part482\"}"}
