{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_655_watany_guide_part652", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part652", "text": "(required docs + forms + audience scope/domain/life event). \nDaleel\n\n \nDaleel\n\nIf you paste me the first ~30 lines of your current apps/gateway-api/src/server.ts (after the script runs), I’ll tell you exactly where the KB boot block landed and how to keep it clean for deployment (prod vs dev).\n\nSources\n\nYou said:\nthe salary is one aspect of the chatbot but the basis of the chatbot should rely on daleel document, on needed files from the mof and laf\n\nChatGPT said:\n\nThought for 13s\nGot it. Salary is just one module. The core Watany chatbot KB should be built around:\n\nDaleel = the “source of truth” for procedures/transactions and what the user must submit.\n\nMOF + LAF attachments = the actual forms/files required by those procedures (PDF/Word/links), saved locally + indexed.\n\nThen you layer salary KB as a separate “calculator KB” module.\n\nBelow is a practical KB strategy + ONE single script you paste in VSCode/Copilot to do everything: map docs, download attachments, rewrite to local, build a deploy-ready KB.\n\nKB strategy (Watany-first)\nA) KB structure (consistent + future-proof)\nCreate data/kb/ with:\n\ndata/kb/runtime_kb.json (one file server loads into app.kb)\n\ndata/kb/json/\n\nprocedures.json ✅ (from Daleel: procedure cards + required docs)\n\nforms_linkmap.json ✅ (from MOF/LAF HTML: url→local mapping)\n\nsources.json ✅ (audit trail: which doc produced which KB items)\n\nsalary/* ✅ (your salary module outputs, separate)\n\ndata/kb/attachments/ ✅ (downloaded PDFs/DOCs from MOF/LAF)\n\ndata/kb/kb.jsonl ✅ (RAG-friendly “chunks” so your chatbot can answer “شو بدي قدّم؟”)\n\nB) What the chatbot answers (core)\nThe chatbot should answer procedural questions first:\n\n“I want X benefit/service → what documents do I need?”\n\n“Which form do I download?”\n\n“Where do I submit?”\n\n“Eligibility & notes”\n\n“Steps”\n\nThen salary is a separate tool route: /api/salary/calc.\n\nC) One KB build pipeline\nIn VSCode:\n\nput Daleel + MOF/LAF HTML + salary docs in doc/\n\nrun node tools/build_watany_kb.js\n\nstart server → it loads data/kb/runtime_kb.json\n\n✅ ONE script to paste in Copilot (Build KB from Daleel + MOF/LAF + attach forms locally)\nSave as: tools/build_watany_kb.js\nRun: node tools/build_watany_kb.js\n\nAssumes these files exist in your repo:\n\ndoc/Daleel.docx\n\ndoc/index.html (MOF page export)\n\ndoc/laf.html (LAF page export)\n\n(optional salary module inputs you already use)\n\n/**\n * tools/build_watany_kb.js\n * Run: node tools/build_watany_kb.js\n *\n * Builds the CORE Watany KB based on:\n * - Daleel.docx (procedures + required docs)\n * - index.html (MOF) + laf.html (LAF) (forms links + attachments)\n *\n * Outputs:\n * - data/kb/attachments/* (downloaded files)\n * - data/kb/json/procedures.json\n * - data/kb/json/forms_linkmap.json\n * - data/kb/kb.jsonl (RAG chunks)\n * - data/kb/runtime_kb.json (single runtime blob server loads into app.kb)\n *\n * Notes:\n * - Downloads can fail if remote blocks bots. Use SKIP_DOWNLOAD=1 to only map links:\n * $env:SKIP_DOWNLOAD=\"1\"", "metadata": "{\"source\": \"watany.txt\", \"keywords\": \"watany_guide_part652\"}"}
{"chunk_id": "knowledge_knowledge_656_watany_guide_part653", "chunk_type": "knowledge", "doc_topic_no": "watany_guide_part653", "text": "; node tools/build_watany_kb.js\n */\n\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst crypto = require(\"node:crypto\");\nconst zlib = require(\"node:zlib\");\n\n// ---------- paths ----------\nconst REPO = process.cwd();\nconst DOC_DIR = path.join(REPO, \"doc\");\nconst OUT_DIR = path.join(REPO, \"data\", \"kb\");\nconst JSON_DIR = path.join(OUT_DIR, \"json\");\nconst ATT_DIR = path.join(OUT_DIR, \"attachments\");\nconst KB_JSONL = path.join(OUT_DIR, \"kb.jsonl\");\nconst RUNTIME_KB = path.join(OUT_DIR, \"runtime_kb.json\");\n\nconst INPUT = {\n daleel: path.join(DOC_DIR, \"Daleel.docx\"),\n mofHtml: path.join(DOC_DIR, \"index.html\"),\n lafHtml: path.join(DOC_DIR, \"laf.html\"),\n};\n\nfunction ensureDir(p) { fs.mkdirSync(p, { recursive: true }); }\nfunction exists(p) { return fs.existsSync(p); }\nfunction readText(p) { return fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\"); }\nfunction writeText(p, s) { ensureDir(path.dirname(p)); fs.writeFileSync(p, s, \"utf8\"); }\nfunction writeJson(p, o) { ensureDir(path.dirname(p)); fs.writeFileSync(p, JSON.stringify(o, null, 2), \"utf8\"); }\nfunction sha1(s) { return crypto.createHash(\"sha1\").update(s).digest(\"hex\"); }\nfunction safeName(s) {\n return String(s || \"\")\n .trim()\n .replace(/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}\\.\\-_ ]/gu, \"\")\n .replace(/\\s+/g, \"_\")\n .slice(0, 160) || (\"file_\" + Math.random().toString(16).slice(2));\n}\nfunction nowISO() { return new Date().toISOString(); }\n\n// ---------- minimal DOCX text extraction ----------\nfunction extractDocxText(docxPath) {\n const buf = fs.readFileSync(docxPath);\n const sig = Buffer.from([0x50, 0x4b, 0x03, 0x04]); // PK..\n let off = 0;\n while (true) {\n off = buf.indexOf(sig, off);\n if (off === -1) break;\n\n const compMethod = buf.readUInt16LE(off + 8);\n const compSize = buf.readUInt32LE(off + 18);\n const fileNameLen